{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank","id":831840,"title":"Mages As Monsters - Discussion, Examples, ThinkTank","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-17T10:01:54-08:00","id":831840,"title":"Mages As Monsters - Discussion, Examples, ThinkTank","content":"So, a few things before we start.<br /> To avoid flamewars and overall toxic atmosphere, I want to make one single rule that I ask everybody here to follow - please, no discussion about semantics of word &quot;Monster&quot; and attempts on Language Imperialism expressed in trying to enforce single, dominating definition of what Monster means. Thank you in advance.<br /> ***<br /> <br /> Inspired by a thread that asked a question about monstrosity of Mages, I want to talk about practical examples of Mages being Monsters. I want to ask you the following:<br /> - What makes Mage a Monster in your eyes?<br /> - Do you have any interesting examples of it? Double points for examples that come from actual play, and especially from player characters<br /> - What abilities, Arcanas, merits, and other gameplay mechanics do you feel make or could make Mages interesting Monsters?<br /> <br /> So, I'll start with an example of one of things that my Soon To Be Character does:<br /> She is a Mage with Time 3, who liked photography a lot even before her Awakening; not that she was very good at it (She has 0 in Expression, but Specialty in Photography to make it work). One of first things she used her new powers was rewinding time to take a shot when she realized that she wasted a good opportunity. However, as she explored the Time magic in context of her work, she found that &quot;just&quot; redoing photos was boring; after learning about ability to shield people and objects from effects of Time Magic, she decided to try out using it on her camera. And alas, it worked! So she started taking not only more photos, but also gathered confidence to do shots that she wouldn't normally do, because...well, she could always rewind time. So she started taking photos of her friends who were always mad that she is waving her camera at her, and rewinding it so they won't get annoyed; she started pulling out camera in her classes at college and captured the professor and his audience, because all of his scolding was never going to happen. And again, this soon became boring; step after step, she started taking more and more daring pictures. Weird questions started probing her mind; wouldn't this church be beautiful soaked in flames? How about taking photos of a car crash? Rewind after rewind, she started pushing her boundaries; <br /> Church was burned down to the earth, but it was fine, because it never happened. A cat drowned, but it was fine, because what really happened was that she saved it. <br /> This, coupled with her training as Guardian of the Veil, lead to some practical habits, too; a lot of her conversations never happened. Lot of books were never read. When somebody doesn't want to cooperate and tell you what you want, all you need to do is to break his legs and rewind. Which also makes a great occasion for a shot! Have you ever photographed a freshly dead person? It also works great as a blackmail material. <br /> But it's all fine. Because it never happened. And never will happen. The choices she leaves as &quot;canon&quot;? Always good ones. Always nice ones. She is a good person, and why does it matter that her photo album is pretty morbid? Photoshop, for sure!<br /> <br /> <br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":23}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T10:28:29-08:00","id":831858,"title":"","content":"First off, I love your character. I had a similar Obrimos Libertine in a game a while back. She used to be a member of Network Zero, and she repeatedly found really good footage of non-Supernal supernatural stuff. Which she'd then basically force onto people. Integrity would have been nice to have back then, but she basically brute forced revelatory experiences into people's lives, sometimes setting up unavoidable encounters with the supernatural.<br /> <br /> Naturally, she watched from the sidelines, making sure nobody was physically injured. It got a lot of people hurt in the long term though, as she threatened to unveil various masquerades and by forcing people to look into the abyss, she was inviting the abyss to look back at her vict...offer...&quot;apprentices.&quot; She was just trying to prime people for their own Awakenings!<br /> <br /> The thing that makes Mages monsters in my eyes is that they combine power with a sense of self-righteousness. Where the self-righteousness comes from is irrelevant: the mages think they know better (because it's arguable that they <i>do</i>), and then they express their power to try to make things like they &quot;should&quot; be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T10:52:37-08:00","id":831877,"title":"","content":"Abuses of the Death Arcana are so stereotypical and obvious as to be barely worth saying.<br /> <br /> But I feel I should mention the &quot;can-it-be-done&quot; question I brought up before, regarding forcing a single individual to be used as a ghost template, again and again (reviving them after each &quot;ghosting&quot;). I feel this necromantic pioneer would get on wonderfully with your &quot;never happened&quot; photographer.<br /> <hr /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank#post831840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- What makes Mage a Monster in your eyes?<br /> - Do you have any interesting examples of it? Double points for examples that come from actual play, and especially from player characters<br /> - What abilities, Arcanas, merits, and other gameplay mechanics do you feel make or could make Mages interesting Monsters?</div> </div> </div> </div>- When a Mage exploits their (relatively) superior power and knowledge in a way that treats others as &quot;lesser&quot;. &quot;They're only Sleepers, Ghosts, Spirits, etc.&quot;.<br /> - Fate-rigging things in your favor. Nothing's free - Everything you &quot;won&quot; cheated someone else out of their chance. Because you felt you deserved it.<br /> - See above with Death. Mind for brainwashing, obviously, though combo-ing it with Spirit(?) to make Goetic &quot;sleeper agents/spies&quot; to seed the area with is also a good example. I'd say the best uses for &quot;interesting monster&quot; stem from potentially benign intent taken to their full horrible implications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 02-17-2016, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T10:54:31-08:00","id":831884,"title":"","content":"One of the things that I did in my game is to codify what it means to be a monster. I drew a line between supernatural and the mundane, and used modifed and updated Atrocity mechanics from Danse Macabre to track what I term the &quot;metaphysical weight&quot; of very harmful deeds done that affect beings with souls. Mundane people lose the equivient of Integrity when their Temporary Atrocity would have caused a supernatural creature to have gained a Permanent Atrocity and indeed if they drop to what would be the equivilent of zero Integrity in my setting they gain a Greater Undertaking of a Slasher (at the equivient of one Integrity they gained the Lesser Undertaking, but this is loss if they rise in Integrity) and thus start track Permanent Atrocity exactly like a supernatural creature. Supernatural creatures in my chronicles also gain Slasher undertakings at the bottom of their Stability Advantages. For those unfamiliar with what Permanent Atrocity, it adds bonuses to supernatural Dicepools and penalties to hiding one's supernatural nature, and thus is a wonderful way to track increasing monstrousness. I tied it into the Personal Bane system to help balance the increase in power with additional weaknesses, because frequently the more monstrous and powerful a character becomes it also seems very thematically correct to have them more riddled with flaws and things that can counter them. Also since I am untethering Personal Banes from the Stability Advantage which now only reflect mental health instead of morality, this better tracks the journey from merely being supernatural to being a monster.<br /> <br /> This of course also applies to Mages, and even minor templates in my chronicles. Picture changing from being just a happy and caring midwife and herbalist with alternative fashion sense to a vile cackling green-skinned hag that devours sweets made from children to absorb their vital energies and souls to power her immortality. (a particular application of an Attainment gained from a very interesting alchemical Legacy which isn't neccisarily evil but is focused on potions and edibles that act as a way to transfer properties from the ingredient to the eater)<br /> <br /> Now mages can be driven to Atrocity most easily by pride and hubris, which certainly is different than being driven to Atrocity by rage and instinct to hunt, or even the undead thirst for blood and savage inner beast, but the slope is just as slippery and easy to fall down and is perhaps easier to start down because the consequences are initially less glaringly horrifying to human sensibilities.<br /> <br /> Yes, mages can be monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-17-2016, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T11:13:21-08:00","id":831894,"title":"","content":"To me, Mages are monstrous for largely the same reasons as the True Fae. Horribly bloated egos, nigh-impenetrable certainty in their own superiority and godlike power. If you need good examples of how awful Mages can be, read about our dear vice-ridden Greek Gods, especially Zeus. The very word <b><a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hubris\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Hubris&quot;</a></b> was coined by the Ancient Greeks.<br /> <br /> For more modern examples, take a look at Voldemort from Harry Potter, Kilgrave from Jessica Jones and Anthony Fremont from the Twilight Zone episode &quot;It's A Good Life&quot;. <br /> <br /> To me, the scariest Arcana are Life, Mind and Death, because they can be used to permanently disfigure and defile people physically, mentally and spiritually. <br /> <br /> I mean, a Mage can straight up subject an innocent person to the same eternal torture that Ted suffers at the end of &quot;I Have No Mouth And I Must Scream&quot;. For even the tiniest perceived slight.<br /> <br /> All of this is perfectly summed up by Gildor in the Fellowship Of The Ring: &quot;Do not meddle in the affairs of wizards, for they are subtle and quick to anger&quot;.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, in the section of the Beast preview about how the Anakim (who are nicknamed Giants and embody the fear of Powerlessness) view other denizens of the CoD, there is the following observation regarding Mages.<br /> <br /> &quot;Remember when I said that not all giants tower physically? I'm talking about these guys.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-17-2016, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T11:41:10-08:00","id":831920,"title":"","content":"In my LARP we brought in an NPC by the name of Adramelech to confront the players about the potential monstrosity they could become. He was an old doctor with a specialty in Child Psychology, member of the Free Council but truly hadn't attended Assembly once in the last 20 years. Awoken as a Mastigos, he became obsessed with determining the process through which children gain their Vices and Virtues. To do so, he took control of an orphanage and created a Demesne in a secret blocked off room behind his medical office. The first experiments weren't too unethical. He put kids to sleep and meditated to explore their Oneiros, noting the degree of development of their Vice and Virtue demons as they grew. <br /> <br /> He noticed that some kids had stronger demons than others, and made several attempts to manipulate their control over the subject. He understood that a Vice demon could be beaten in the Oneiros, and this caused beneficial effects in the children's conduct. However, the change was never permanent, either a new Vice would develop or the previous Vice would respawn like a cancer. He also noted that Vice demons could be defeated more easily the younger the kid was, as long as one had already developed. Finding the precise timing to attack the demon led to the best results, but as of yet, he could not make them permanent. He took up the study of Death, interested in examining the Integrity of his subjects after and before the experiments.<br /> <br /> By chance, he ran into a kid that had some particularly dark experiences from a dark age, probably due to supernatural possession of some sort couple with parental abuse. He observed a correlation between Integrity damage and Vices which had only be theoretical from his studies up to this point. He later learned to adjust his Mage Sight to see this correlation on any subject he wished. He used some influences to get his hands on some tomes of Reaper lore from the Mysterium, which contained detailed accounts on the effects of Soul damage. He decided that maybe he could more closely examine the Soul to figure out the connection he needed, as at this point Oneiros exploration seemed like a dead end. <br /> <br /> With a heavy heart at first, he began experimenting with the removal of children's souls, followed by thorough scrutiny, putting them back carefully and comparing observations with psychological profiles and Oneiros exploration. After several years of work, he compiled a lengthy thesis: he had found the part of the Soul in which Vices are anchored. This part of the soul could be intentionally damaged to prevent Vices from forming, but it must be performed at an early age, before the Vice fully becomes part of their personality. His very first attempt at the procedure was a complete success. He created human beings entirely free of Vice. He repeated his procedure more than 50 times and basically created a new Reaper Legacy.<br /> <br /> The procedure though had a few negative consequences, of course. Removing the damaged soul would allow the Vice to manifest (as per the normal soulless condition) but if this happened after several years of living without the Vice, it could dry the subject mad with an intense uncontrollable Vice, as they never had any practice resisting it. Inserting a new fresh soul at this stage didn't help much either, the personality would still be flawed. Of course, Adramelech considered this to be a minor flaw: after all, if you get your soul removed, you are probably already fucked. No reason to worry so much about that small corner case, where there could be such a great benefit to society to remove the Vices of potential rapists and assassins. There were other consequences which Adramelech probably noticed but chose to disregard, to the point of never even documenting, such as a higher suicide rate among subjects, irrational behavior when dealing with the Vices of others, strange phenomena in the Oneiros, and so far none of those kids have managed to Awaken or become Sleepwalkers. <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Now, even though people starting knowing about this guy for a few months, few Mages were interested in going up against him, they always had excuses about bigger fish to fry and so forth. However, he later became entangled in Concilium business for an entirely different reason: a suspected connection between Mysterium corruption (which was true) and the possesion of an Artifact which was believed stolen (which was a lie). After a couple of confrontations, the Adamantine Arrow took over his Demesne and expelled him from the city (the city Councilors wanted him dead of course, but the Arrow had a few issues with the Councilors at the time, and thus decided to just expel him to spite them). And then the Arrow took the Demesne as theirs as well as his library, including his masterpiece: the Grimoire which he transcribed after his many experiments, detailing not only the spells used, but the precise method in which they needed to be combined in order to permanently rid a small child of their Vice. A note found on the Grimoire indicated that this was a copy, and that it was intended as a gift to his old friend from the Mysterium which helped him learn more about Souls. The Arrow decided not to surrender the Grimoire to the Mysterium, and is still unsure on keeping it or destroying it, but a few members hope it might come useful. As to the previous patients, some have been found, many are dead, and one Mage who set out to investigate seems to be missing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T12:25:13-08:00","id":831966,"title":"","content":"With addition to agreeing pretty much with everyone's posts above me, I think mages suffer from a problem many comic superheroes often have to deal with as well. I'm talking about the individual/persona divide.<br /> <br /> Almost every superhero has a secret identity, but they are quite obviously individuals as well. Many stories have dealt with superheroes trying to find a sense of balance between their personal and &quot;professional&quot; life. Regardless of how it ends (or it doesn't), the biggest problem in this struggle I see is that while superheroes are individuals, the superhero personas are, well, <i>symbols</i>. No credit is given for guessing how a person becomes a mage. Yes, that's correct, by making their name a symbol etched into the foundation of reality itself.<br /> <br /> Their *name*. They don't just get a costume, <i>that</i> creates already enough identity trouble. No, they *are* an amalgam of a symbol and an individual, a bridge across the abyss between a man and something greater, with the purpose of their life being to cross to the other side, with steps across that bridge, across <b>themselves</b>, happening with every move, every thought they make and imagine. They cannot take comfort in taking off the mask, not really.<br /> <br /> They cannot *stop*, no matter what they tell themselves. It is no wonder many falter, many fall. Without knowing themselves, knowing who they are, what their true goal, true purpose, true <i>name</i> is, they cannot ever understand what they desire, to ever truly succeed. Their actions won't resonate with their name, and the bridge that they are will *shatter*, a slow death, one shard at the time until only a phantom of their true selves, a husk, a <b>tulpa</b>, will be all that's left.<br /> <br /> All of them fall. If only they understood. If only they remained true to themselves, they could cross. If they were true to their name, if <i>one</i> was, the bridge could be crossed, action and symbol, intent and name, united.<br /> <br /> And the world would be as they are. One again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 02-17-2016, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T12:44:37-08:00","id":831986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=831966#post831966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With addition to agreeing pretty much with everyone's posts above me, I think mages suffer from a problem many comic superheroes often have to deal with as well. I'm talking about the individual/persona divide.<br /> <br /> Almost every superhero has a secret identity, but they are quite obviously individuals as well. Many stories have dealt with superheroes trying to find a sense of balance between their personal and &quot;professional&quot; life. Regardless of how it ends (or it doesn't), the biggest problem in this struggle I see is that while superheroes are individuals, the superhero personas are, well, <i>symbols</i>. No credit is given for guessing how a person becomes a mage. Yes, that's correct, by making their name a symbol etched into the foundation of reality itself.<br /> <br /> Their *name*. They don't just get a costume, <i>that</i> creates already enough identity trouble. No, they *are* an amalgam of a symbol and an individual, a bridge across the abyss between a man and something greater, with the purpose of their life being to cross to the other side, with steps across that bridge, across <b>themselves</b>, happening with every move, every thought they make and imagine. They cannot take comfort in taking off the mask, not really.<br /> <br /> They cannot *stop*, no matter what they tell themselves. It is no wonder many falter, many fall. Without knowing themselves, knowing who they are, what their true goal, true purpose, true <i>name</i> is, they cannot ever understand what they desire, to ever truly succeed. Their actions won't resonate with their name, and the bridge that they are will *shatter*, a slow death, one shard at the time until only a phantom of their true selves, a husk, a <b>tulpa</b>, will be all that's left.<br /> <br /> All of them fall. If only they understood. If only they remained true to themselves, they could cross. If they were true to their name, if <i>one</i> was, the bridge could be crossed, action and symbol, intent and name, united.<br /> <br /> And the world would be as they are. One again.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like your choice of words. The use of Tulpa is interesting to me because that's the term used in 2ED for <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/sympathy-for-the-sinister/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>one of the many horrible drawbacks of being Mad.</b></a> Was that intentional?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T12:46:35-08:00","id":831988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=831986#post831986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I like your choice of words. The use of Tulpa is interesting to me because that's the term used in 2ED for <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/sympathy-for-the-sinister/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>one of the many horrible drawbacks of being Mad.</b></a> Was that intentional?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. Tulpa also means &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tulpa\" target=\"_blank\">phantom</a>&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T12:48:02-08:00","id":831989,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=831920#post831920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">cool stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very interesting. My group is currently investigating a plot about Echo Walkers; to summarize it, they noticed increased suicide rate and found out that some souls were misaligned lately. Three Echo Walkers that are in the city are a Priest (who uses the dislodge soul at people during their confessions, as god's punishment in hope that they will feel smitten enough to change their behavior; then he realigns them), a Psychologist (who experiments upon his patients, but aligns their souls afterwards), and a hospital MD (who uses it on patients that are not going to wake up, or are under sedation, and also realigns them). Of the three, mr Psychologist is probably going to be the weakest link and one who will surrender if they find him out. Why I'm talking about this?<br /> I'm kinda interested in using the plot you talked about later, and I will probably use the Psychologist as a potential link and clues-source for *that* investigation. Would you be mad if I borrowed ideas of Adramalech for my Chronicle?<br /> ***<br /> Serial-Ghoster sounds scary and creepy. I like it! One of our NPCs, Mr.Smith, does something similar; he uses *himself* as a template for Ghosts he creates using Making Death, and then incorporates them into dead bodies/zombies. This gives him minions that don't even need mind controlling, because they *are* copies of himself, so their interests are his interests! While they obviusly don't inherent his magical powers, they are still a pretty nice ghosts in terms of power.<br /> It also amuses me greatly, because while one of my players made a deal with Mr.Smith and became kind of his ally, not all Ghost-Smiths know about it; I'm going to enjoy the confusion that will happen when she will run into one of projects overseen by GhostSmith who will not recognize her at all and will actually try to eradicate her.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> The &quot;look THIS IS PROOF!&quot; Obrimos is cool. It kinda inspired me for some thinking about Awakening Gambit and their possible projects and MO's. I love that Legacy, it can lead into massive Hubris. I don't care much about their Arcanas, because as a GM I will just handwave it as a &quot;developed their own version of it&quot;, because I don't feel that their Arcanas and Attaiments are actually relevant to their core identity at all (YMMV).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T13:47:26-08:00","id":832035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=831989#post831989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Serial-Ghoster sounds scary and creepy. I like it! One of our NPCs, Mr.Smith, does something similar; he uses *himself* as a template for Ghosts he creates using Making Death, and then incorporates them into dead bodies/zombies. This gives him minions that don't even need mind controlling, because they *are* copies of himself, so their interests are his interests! While they obviusly don't inherent his magical powers, they are still a pretty nice ghosts in terms of power.<br /> It also amuses me greatly, because while one of my players made a deal with Mr.Smith and became kind of his ally, not all Ghost-Smiths know about it; I'm going to enjoy the confusion that will happen when she will run into one of projects overseen by GhostSmith who will not recognize her at all and will actually try to eradicate her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. It was a thought experiment developed after the discussion regarding &quot;What are souls?&quot; a while back. Before I knew Death could just create ghosts ex nihilo (sort of). The ideas was take the Template, cast Quicken Ghost, have a Demon kill them, then use Raise Dead for repeating the cycle. Memory editing recommended, though optional. Use additional editing with Death, to taste.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to extend the madness, have them team up with an Idigam and see what happens when you have a person Hive-Claimed by a bunch of their own ghosts. Bound to be something interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T14:20:13-08:00","id":832064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=831989#post831989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you be mad if I borrowed ideas of Adramalech for my Chronicle?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, go crazy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T22:52:21-08:00","id":832336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank#post831840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, a few things before we start.<br /> To avoid flamewars and overall toxic atmosphere, I want to make one single rule that I ask everybody here to follow - please, no discussion about semantics of word &quot;Monster&quot; and attempts on Language Imperialism expressed in trying to enforce single, dominating definition of what Monster means. Thank you in advance.<br /> ***<br /> <br /> Inspired by a thread that asked a question about monstrosity of Mages, I want to talk about practical examples of Mages being Monsters. I want to ask you the following:<br /> - What makes Mage a Monster in your eyes?<br /> - Do you have any interesting examples of it? Double points for examples that come from actual play, and especially from player characters<br /> - What abilities, Arcanas, merits, and other gameplay mechanics do you feel make or could make Mages interesting Monsters?<br /> <br /> So, I'll start with an example of one of things that my Soon To Be Character does:<br /> She is a Mage with Time 3, who liked photography a lot even before her Awakening; not that she was very good at it (She has 0 in Expression, but Specialty in Photography to make it work). One of first things she used her new powers was rewinding time to take a shot when she realized that she wasted a good opportunity. However, as she explored the Time magic in context of her work, she found that &quot;just&quot; redoing photos was boring; after learning about ability to shield people and objects from effects of Time Magic, she decided to try out using it on her camera. And alas, it worked! So she started taking not only more photos, but also gathered confidence to do shots that she wouldn't normally do, because...well, she could always rewind time. So she started taking photos of her friends who were always mad that she is waving her camera at her, and rewinding it so they won't get annoyed; she started pulling out camera in her classes at college and captured the professor and his audience, because all of his scolding was never going to happen. And again, this soon became boring; step after step, she started taking more and more daring pictures. Weird questions started probing her mind; wouldn't this church be beautiful soaked in flames? How about taking photos of a car crash? Rewind after rewind, she started pushing her boundaries; <br /> Church was burned down to the earth, but it was fine, because it never happened. A cat drowned, but it was fine, because what really happened was that she saved it. <br /> This, coupled with her training as Guardian of the Veil, lead to some practical habits, too; a lot of her conversations never happened. Lot of books were never read. When somebody doesn't want to cooperate and tell you what you want, all you need to do is to break his legs and rewind. Which also makes a great occasion for a shot! Have you ever photographed a freshly dead person? It also works great as a blackmail material. <br /> But it's all fine. Because it never happened. And never will happen. The choices she leaves as &quot;canon&quot;? Always good ones. Always nice ones. She is a good person, and why does it matter that her photo album is pretty morbid? Photoshop, for sure!<br /> <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice monster, now add in Fate to make sure your girl gets the picture she wants perfectly right on the spot. Who cares about that curse she did on the crowd. Imagine it's my Sasha, Obrimos Forces/Prime/Fate with a bit of Time/Space and Mind. She gets the perfect photo and much more anytime. Is it bad to make the audience's actual desires be the truth? She's what I call a classic witch and how I built both my Verbena and Obrimos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 02-18-2016, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T08:12:47-08:00","id":835063,"title":"","content":"Ah, but she cares. She would never ever cast a curse on random people with intent of letting it stay. She finds it horrible and repulsive. It's kind of a denial mechanism here; she thinks that because she rewinds, it's harmless and not-wrong. And because she can slip into her Mask during the &quot;Interrogation Rewind Session&quot;, her Wisdom can be maintained, too.<br /> If it was ever revealed that each Rewind leaves a standalone, still continuing timeline, she would be *devastated*.<br /> <br /> Another spell I want to work with is possibly Words of Truth from Prime 2 (which means I might end up having Acanthus with Prime 2, or Obrimos with Time 3, or get either Shifting Sands or Words of Truth as artifact, unless something in other Arcanas will catch my eye). I really like write ups of spells in Mage, because while yeah it's all about improvisation yada yada, pre-estabilished spells often provide me with instant inspiration, just add mana <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> EDIT<br /> Or Moros with camera loaded with Shifting Sands, Words of Truth and considered to be shield-of-chronosed. Depends on rules, but I kinda like idea of artifact that allows you to say TRUE TRUTH OF TRUTHNESS if you have photo evidence to back it up.<br /> <br /> So, Words of Truth: as long as statement is true, and you believe it to be true, you can channel the true-ness so hard it cannot be refused. I feel that this spell, even if it's effectively certain kind of mind control, is distinct enough to make a character who considers mind control immoral, consider this spell O-K.<br /> Basically, it helps others see the truth. It can help people! Finally, you can tell your little brother that eating veggies IS GOOD FOR HIS HEALTH, you can persuade the cop that they *should* investigate this person, and of course there is potential for classical detective showdown where our mage gathers all the suspects, explains her reasoning, and then points a finger at the criminal speaking the Words of Truth that yes, you are the murderer!<br /> I can see this spells as a great temptation for those that are not very good in social matters, who feel that their words need extra weight and who feel small. This spell allows them to rely on outside authority, and might transform a shrinking violet into righteous knight.<br /> There is a plethora of situations in everyday life where this spell can really help - it can help you to show your sister that her boyfriend is a cheating bastard, it can comfort someone who is afraid that their friend died mad at them for words they said during their last meeting, it can win you arguments and help other people see the truth. Which, of course, can and will cause breaking points, and the &quot;righteous use&quot; and &quot;abuse&quot; are really hard to distinguish with this spell.<br /> For my character, she will probably be the shrinking violet kind, one who uses it to make herself sure of her own words and to compensate for lacking self confidence. But with the Mask and Time-Fuckery of photos...a very nasty usage of Words of Truth I imagine could work:<br /> Make impossible photos. Then state that YES, THIS PHOTO IS UNTAMPERED WITH IN ANY WAY. I MADE IT WITH MY OWN CAMERA, AND IT CAPTURED A REAL THING. NO PHOTOSHOP OR OTHER TRICKERY INCLUDED. Which, of course, can boost her prestige as a photographer, but also allows for a very, very horrible perversion that might evolve from her guardian mask:<br /> &quot;This is a picture of your dead body. I took it myself and there was no tampering included with the photo, it really is real. This is your blood, and this is your bone; I took them out with my tools. [insert a lot of descriptions that confirm reality of different wounds, different icky details, and their source] This photo is real and it really captures a scene where I mercilessly killed you. &quot;<br /> I really love the fact that if you figure out a signature behavior like this, you can put it into a mask and be like ka-tching! Wisdom saved!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 02-22-2016, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T16:40:17-08:00","id":840246,"title":"","content":"Some more brainstorming on the Words of Truth.<br /> Having ability to cast this spell should create a cascade of potential Breaking Points. Good thing Mages don't bother with Integrity! But, you ask - why?<br /> Hear me out.<br /> <br /> Words of Truth gives you ability to speak a sentence that is absolutely, objectively true. All you need is to fully believe that it's true, and it to be true. Simple as that. So, logically, it also means that you may not, as part of this spell, speak a sentence that is either:<br /> a) objectively not-true<br /> b) in which you don't fully, truly believe.<br /> So, as long as you have absolute certainity and something and are right, you can say it out loud. If you are not certain, or it is untrue, you may not say it. This allows you to check certain things...for example, can you say things like:<br /> &quot;My significant other loves me&quot;, &quot;My parents are happy that I was born&quot;, &quot;My life has meaning&quot;, &quot;I love my boyfriend&quot;, &quot;I would never betray my friends&quot;, &quot;I'm a good person&quot;, &quot;I did everything I could to save him&quot;, and so on?<br /> If you they are true and you believe, you can say it. If it's untrue and you believe it, you can't say it. If it's true and you don't believe hard enough, you can't say it. Would you have guts to try answering questions that would pop up in dark corners of your mind?<br /> I don't know about you, but if I had such ability, it would drive me insane with anxiety and fear. The fact that you can't really know if the statement failed because it's false, or because you are of little faith nails the coffin for me.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Spell text for easy access<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/572895-2e-spell-spoiler-compilation?p=572938#post572938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#008080\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b><u><i>Prime</i></u></b></span></span></div><br /> <br /> <b>Words of Truth (Prime </b>\u2022\u2022 <b>)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Spell Factor:</b> Scale (Targets)<br /> <b>Rote Skills: </b>Expression, Intimidation. Persuasion<br /> The mage speaks with tongues of fire, and the world listens. So long as the words the mage speaks are objectively true and the mage herself believes them whole-heartedly, all subjects of this spell can hear and understand her clearly, regardless of distance, noise, or language barriers. Moreover, all subjects know, on a soul-deep level, that what the mage says is true. This doesn\u2019t necessarily compel them to act on that information, but ignoring or refuting this Supernal truth may be grounds for a Breaking Point. In a Social Maneuvering action, this spell may remove one door or improve reaction level by one step per level of Potency.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage\u2019s words don\u2019t merely ring with truth, but call to action. If a subject goes along with what the mage said, they gain the Inspired Condition. If they ignore it, they gain the Guilty Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-01-2016, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:13:40-08:00","id":840269,"title":"","content":"Why believing something strongly is a requirement for it? Which one supersedes the other clause?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:15:43-08:00","id":840272,"title":"","content":"I have an example from actual play, involving a character who, by the end of the arc it occurred in, was terrified that her own existence as an Awakened was one doomed to end in monstrosity.<br /> <br /> The short of it is that her family line was tied to a... Thing in a small town. I don't have a name or word for it; it was just the very literal heart of the place; a throbbing, pulsating, luminous heart, suspended from vines in the centre of a hollow chamber filled with trees that grew in absence of sunlight. Whatever it was, it was sapient, friendly, and driven mad by fear of its waning consciousness and the thoughts of being trapped forever. For about 160 years, it subtly manipulated her family, herself included, to the point that she found out she was likely born as a part of its grand design.<br /> <br /> Before this ever reached a conclusion, though, she discovered she was a monster.<br /> <br /> In investigating her family tree, she discovered why her mother left her home town, and why her uncle stayed; why she'd never known her maternal grandparents. The latter had died in a house fire, and left the former to raise his younger sister alone. Cue the young Thyrsus, on investigating, finding out that it was not the fire that killed her grandparents, but a knife; a knife with a strong sympathetic link to her uncle.<br /> <br /> The whole climax involved her confronting her uncle one rainy night; taking the form of a terrible feathered beast and wrecking his car; using torrents of water to pin him in place, setting an axe to his neck, and...<br /> <br /> Hearing he'd done it to save his sister.<br /> <br /> It was a pretty powerful moment. It was an instant of realization of just what kind of power she wields; just how badly she could hurt people if she wanted to, without repercussion. A few words were all that kept her from becoming a murderer.<br /> <br /> Not the first or last time she did things like that either; unleashing a pack of wolves on someone slandering her friend (just to scare him), breaking a police officer's arm, tormenting a spirit into obedience...<br /> <br /> She always had good reasons for everything she did, but none of it excuses her. She had power and, rather than reacting sensibly and cautiously, lashed out passionately.<br /> <br /> Mages are powerful people and, like all powerful people, have a choice in how they use their power. If they're self-controlled and compassionate, they can be noble and awe-inspiring. Humans aren't always either of those things, though, and those lesser moments can shape lives. Even simple ignorance can ruin otherwise noble aims and potentials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:37:29-08:00","id":840279,"title":"","content":"Powerful, <i>powerful </i>story there Axel. Thank you for sharing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T18:34:01-08:00","id":840299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=840269#post840269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why believing something strongly is a requirement for it? Which one supersedes the other clause?</div> </div> </div> </div>So you can't use it to find the objective truth to any and all questions you might have. If you didn't have to wholeheartedly believe in what you were saying you could literally tell anyone anything using the spell and receive confirmation as to whether or not what you said is true or not depending on whether the spell worked or not. With it written the way it is, it only works if both clauses are true. You believe what you're saying <i>and</i> it is objectively true.<br /> <br /> So instead of being able to use it on a buddy to figure out if aliens are real or anything else that you may or may not be sure of, it's a spell to be used to proclaim facts you know with 100% certainty to be true in a way that no one can deny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T10:18:55-08:00","id":840753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=840279#post840279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Powerful, <i>powerful </i>story there Axel. Thank you for sharing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I just wish I'd structured it better, but that's what you get for writing on a phone.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T15:47:10-07:00","id":848450,"title":"","content":"Some Obsessions/Inspirations to pursue:<br /> <br /> - Wanting to see a precise moment of death while under a Mage Sight and Knowing spells. There is already a lot of non-Mage people wanting to experience it; imagine what a powerful experience it might be when your perception is expanded with Magic. And because it never stops expanding, you will *never see everything there is to be seen*, so you want to see *people dying* and in *different ways* and in *different conditions*...<br /> <br /> - Wanting to find people who experience emotions in different way than you. It's very hard to invent &quot;new&quot; emotions and thus, put them into your Imago; and by new, I mean things that you haven't experienced yourself. If you can invoke joy of eating pizza at will, it may become boring. And if joys of eating pizza and joy of first kiss are different &quot;objects&quot;, you might want to find as much of them as possible, to expand your emotional vocabulary. While this might be noble and bright at first, there is a lot of people taking pleasure in really different ways, with some of them possibly disturbing; and because you want to *feel it with them*, you might want to arrange things for them. And, obviously, because new emotions are new, you might want to experience things like fear, pain and terror by proxy too. <br /> This one, obviously, hinges a lot of your interpretation of how forging a Imago works; if you rule that you can simply go &quot;Ok, I wan't to feel emotion X I never experienced and can't really imagine&quot;, then it doesn't really work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T02:07:56-07:00","id":848687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=848450#post848450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Obsessions/Inspirations to pursue:<br /> <br /> - Wanting to see a precise moment of death while under a Mage Sight and Knowing spells. There is already a lot of non-Mage people wanting to experience it; imagine what a powerful experience it might be when your perception is expanded with Magic. And because it never stops expanding, you will *never see everything there is to be seen*, so you want to see *people dying* and in *different ways* and in *different conditions*...<br /> <br /> - Wanting to find people who experience emotions in different way than you. It's very hard to invent &quot;new&quot; emotions and thus, put them into your Imago; and by new, I mean things that you haven't experienced yourself. If you can invoke joy of eating pizza at will, it may become boring. And if joys of eating pizza and joy of first kiss are different &quot;objects&quot;, you might want to find as much of them as possible, to expand your emotional vocabulary. While this might be noble and bright at first, there is a lot of people taking pleasure in really different ways, with some of them possibly disturbing; and because you want to *feel it with them*, you might want to arrange things for them. And, obviously, because new emotions are new, you might want to experience things like fear, pain and terror by proxy too.<br /> This one, obviously, hinges a lot of your interpretation of how forging a Imago works; if you rule that you can simply go &quot;Ok, I wan't to feel emotion X I never experienced and can't really imagine&quot;, then it doesn't really work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, as a mage, I would like to to go to a sleepwalker on their deathbed, cast as many mage sights on them as I could, link our senses, then experience everything that that person does as they fade away. Who knows, maybe you might get a brief glimpse of the other side. Now I personally would be willing to wait and experience this naturally, though I could easily imagine someone with less scruples arranging an 'unfortunate accident' in order to study such things in a more timely fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-17-2016, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T05:24:31-07:00","id":848720,"title":"","content":"Why would you search for a Sleepwalker specifically? To ask for consent? In some states of USA, if you don't care about consent of person you are &quot;looking at while they die&quot;, it opens up an interesting (and grim) possibility; a Mage who travels all around the USA to witness executions, in order to get their &quot;fix&quot; in a &quot;morally justified&quot; way. Witnessing an execution is imho also a very good moment to throw Awakening at someone, as it fits pretty much every Watchtower in a different way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T05:36:07-07:00","id":848727,"title":"","content":"Suicide Squad, Mage edition? The cabal is formed from former death-row prisioners, but the Consilium has secured their release... if they just do them a few favors...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T06:25:52-07:00","id":848748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=848720#post848720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you search for a Sleepwalker specifically? To ask for consent?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it relates to their state of existence where they're more attuned to the Supernatural than normal people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T08:02:21-07:00","id":848798,"title":"","content":"I figured it would just be because you could cast as many spells on a Sleepwalker as you want without risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T09:31:44-07:00","id":848835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=848727#post848727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suicide Squad, Mage edition? The cabal is formed from former death-row prisioners, but the Consilium has secured their release... if they just do them a few favors...</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always wanted to do a story with Mage who Awakened literally during his execution, which ended his Sleeper life and started Awakened one. I'm not sure if it would be better if everyone thought he really died and his price for new chance at life would be being a no-person with no connections to anyone or anything, or being a fugitive who escaped from a death chamber and is on WANTED posters. Both seems like traumatic and fun experiences to roleplay, providing different sets of challenge to overcome, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T10:24:00-07:00","id":848860,"title":"","content":"Just watching people die is creepy, but hardly monstrous. Not unless you speed it along. No-one started a lynch mob for Duncan MacDougall.<br /> <br /> A small example of monstrosity coming from good intentions: A Moros player of mine has managed to become the bane of police forces across the United States.<br /> <br /> The Moros is generally a fairly noble guy. He's just... Not great at clean-up. A reaper wandered into his town and murdered three teenagers to draw the Moros's mentor out of hiding. He helped her put a very final stop to the reaper, but never revealed it to the public. The result was the local sheriff suspecting the Moros - a newcomer to the area - who'd been caught making out in the graveyard a few weeks before and worked in the area of the murders.<br /> <br /> Later on, he adopted a small Changeling girl and swore an oath to help her find her parents, but her parents weren't exactly great people; they used their daughter as a begging tool and a drug mule. He loved the kid and basicallly gave up on his duty to her. He overlooked an attempted artifact theft by a cult in exchange for their influence in getting her legally adopted by him. The oath broke and his life was exposed; tax evasion, fraudulent adoption papers, bribery, etc.<br /> <br /> But then he just claimed to be an international treasure hunter, put himself in the pocket of a Mastigos lawyer, and managed to get the majority of the charges dropped over lack of evidence (followed by a huge payment in back taxes). He lost his job but managed to retain custody through reapplication of blackmail.<br /> <br /> So now the town sheriff is left looking at a man he suspects of murder and possible child abuse (not a huge leap, seeing how he was accused of basically buying legal guardianship). He's got no evidence, but the guy's squarely in his sights.<br /> <br /> The Necromancer is a decent guy, in intention if nothing else, but he's at the heart of a shitstorm. If he doesn't let the sheriff in on the secret, the guy's going to edge closer and closer to not caring about law and order.<br /> <br /> Part of it's just the sheriff being a xenophobe, but it ain't all undeserved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T10:36:22-07:00","id":848867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=848835#post848835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always wanted to do a story with Mage who Awakened literally during his execution, which ended his Sleeper life and started Awakened one. I'm not sure if it would be better if everyone thought he really died and his price for new chance at life would be being a no-person with no connections to anyone or anything, or being a fugitive who escaped from a death chamber and is on WANTED posters. Both seems like traumatic and fun experiences to roleplay, providing different sets of challenge to overcome, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, pulling multiple posts together, you could have the &quot;Death Voyeur&quot; Mage as part of the Consilium. While carrying out their &quot;research&quot; they happen upon a number of individuals who Awaken during their executions. At first, they save them (be it through stopping the execution, or through a kind of &quot;play dead&quot; spell) because, hey, they are fellow Awakened. Then the Consilium hatches the ideas &quot;Hey, these are convicted major criminals. They are likely to be an even bigger danger Awakened. On the other hand, we have a serious, dangerous problem that needs solving. If we throw them at it, it's win-win. They solve it or die in the attempt, and either outcome removes one of our complications.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T10:40:31-07:00","id":848868,"title":"","content":"Death Voyeurs? More like Stone Scribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T15:50:19-07:00","id":849015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank#post831840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's all fine. Because it never happened. And never will happen. The choices she leaves as &quot;canon&quot;? Always good ones. Always nice ones. She is a good person, and why does it matter that her photo album is pretty morbid? Photoshop, for sure!</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww love it ^.^ definite thumbs up, have you been playing &quot;life is strange&quot;? Seems inspired by it I did love that game myself.<br /> <br /> It's a incredibly dark (World of darkness) take on Max Caufield. Exaggerating the worst elements of her personality upto 11.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4641-pebbles","name":"Pebbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T16:15:37-07:00","id":849026,"title":"","content":"Was freshly after playing it when I cooked that up, yeah. As for it being Dark Max - idea of her being inspired and held captive of phrase and ideology behind &quot;Seriously though, I could frame any one of you in a dark corner, and capture you in a moment of desperation&quot; was very chilling and exciting for me.<br /> As for her Shadow Name, I think that Canon/Kanon is a perfect fit - referencing both actual meaning of word canon, and the camera brand. You could also possibly pass it as a first or last name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T18:39:36-07:00","id":849065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=848720#post848720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you search for a Sleepwalker specifically? To ask for consent? In some states of USA, if you don't care about consent of person you are &quot;looking at while they die&quot;, it opens up an interesting (and grim) possibility; a Mage who travels all around the USA to witness executions, in order to get their &quot;fix&quot; in a &quot;morally justified&quot; way. Witnessing an execution is imho also a very good moment to throw Awakening at someone, as it fits pretty much every Watchtower in a different way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said sleepwalkers specifically so that I wouldn't have to worry about any abyssal shards skewing my results. I'd probably also do the same test using sleeper and, if I could somehow manage it, another mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T05:10:06-07:00","id":849200,"title":"","content":"I see. What would you do if it was clear that each death is a unique event determined by a very large amount of personalized factors combined with outside factors? Would you look for patterns, or look to check out as many and as different people to see dying?<br /> What would you do if you met a person whose qualities would, based on your research, lead to Death unlike anything you experienced before?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T06:07:18-07:00","id":849212,"title":"","content":"I ran a short-lived solo game for an Acanthus artist; she Awakened by changing her own history in such a way that it prevented her death from touching a cursed artifact. Problem was, she didn't remember her new life... And neither did her Sleepwalker friend.<br /> <br /> No-one believes me that this was a coincidence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T14:22:52-07:00","id":849452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=849200#post849200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. What would you do if it was clear that each death is a unique event determined by a very large amount of personalized factors combined with outside factors? Would you look for patterns, or look to check out as many and as different people to see dying?<br /> What would you do if you met a person whose qualities would, based on your research, lead to Death unlike anything you experienced before?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would, undoubtedly, try to study as many cases of Death as I could. The more samples I could get the better. If I noticed any patterns during such research then all the better. If I met someone who would lead to something new I would probably cast some sort of long term death postponement spell, something to keep them at the edge of death, but not crossing that threshold before I could get there and set up. Actually, I'd probably do that with about half of my subjects, and test to see how that influences what they experience. I'd probably need to test it first to see how humane it was, because being held at the threshold of dying yet unable to pass might be especially cruel in some situations. Though if it were adequately acceptable that would be helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T18:34:23-07:00","id":852724,"title":"","content":"Imagine if, when watching a horror movie and munching on popcorn, instead of just shouting at your television &quot;Don't go through that door!&quot; you could actually MAKE THEM not go through that door, and instead get in their car and drive away? In saving their life from what would surely have otherwise been a grisly death, you're the hero, right? Similarly, imagine if you could keep an eye on a large number of situations simultaneously, watching over people, and when they were going to stray from the proper path, you could just force them to make superior decisions. Free will is nice and all, but people are dumb and make the wrong choice all the time, so what's wrong with helping them out and coaxing / forcing them in the right direction?<br /> <br /> That is the struggle the Mastigos face, and when someone with such a powerful and focused will is burdened with knowing what people are thinking, with their fears and indecision and pansy attitudes, it often seems easier just to bring the situation to an expedient resolution. No, you don't need another glass of 'liquid courage', that girl over there has been wondering when you're going to make your move, so it's time to step up and begin the conversation. Heck, let's even break the ice for you and get things flowing. No you're not just going to sit there stewing over your own cowardice and accept the bully's taunts. You're going to get in there and start swinging, and who knows, maybe you even have a shot. Win or lose though, at least you'll respect yourself more tomorrow.<br /> <br /> The Warlock not only sees into other's minds to witness them cowering within their shells, they have the power to willfully drag them out of those selfsame shells and into the light of day. Ceative memory modification means the target in question is left with the memory of his inner voices and demons working him up to the decision instead of his constant badgering and self doubt, and has no reason to believe his choice to act was anything other than his own breakthrough. Who knows, in addition to giving them the courage and impetus to act, the Warlock may well be changing their life for the better.<br /> <br /> Of course, from an outsider's standpoint, a sentient being is dominated, their free will stripped away, and their decision making ability is replaced with someone else's. The Warlock may not stick around long enough to see that relationship crash and burn and the spurned lover commit suicide. He may not see the bully extract his revenge on the person who dared to stand up to him, over the course of months and years to come. He need not burden himself with philosophical questions as to whether someone who, left to their own devices, did not have the courage to see a course of action through is truly ready to deal with the ramifications of those actions. All he need worry about is that in the here and now, the person STOPs their incessant bitching and whining and STEPS UP to the course of action they are contemplating. It's not about the peace that such domination brings to the mental airwaves the Warlock is sampling though. Naturally he would not be so selfish. He's doing them a favor. Honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11463,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11463-giant-octopodes","user":"Giant Octopodes","date":". 03-24-2016, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11463-giant-octopodes","name":"Giant Octopodes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T18:25:25-07:00","id":854293,"title":"","content":"Emotional Urging is a Mastigos best friend. Then again Breaking the Mind Vault as an inured spell might even be better than having it as an attainment like the Reality Walker guys. <br /> <br /> At least that choice still incurs paradox and thus trust from your fellow mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T18:27:59-07:00","id":854297,"title":"","content":"It only risks Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T18:54:56-07:00","id":854306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=854297#post854297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It only risks Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which one? I'm under the impression Emotional Urging should rarely if ever risk paradox. Breaching the Mind Vault usually would unless used in ritual time w/o sleepers around. And likely could be done pretty safely even with 1 or 2 sleepers right there. Like in a doctor office, lab, or in the local witch doctor's hut depending on which reality zone you reside in. <br /> <br /> If it isn't obvious then there isn't paradox. Hence the reason why the FC is the biggest faction. They understand sleeper culture has secrets and it can be worked with but it takes a level of effort that isn't usually worth it in a game. Or more exactly any game I care about.<br /> <br /> I like using magic and suffering the consequences. What can I tell you.<br /> <br /> To me the different versions of Mage are pretty straightforward and about James Bond vs. The Matrix. Superheroes vs. The Man. While in MtAw it's pretty clear it's someone that understands it's all a lie to enable the 1% pure and simple, for me the game isn't about culture because that is the rabbit hole that has gotten us here. It's all about Control vs. Freedom. Tyranny and Envy vs. Democracy and Trust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 03-27-2016, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T19:09:30-07:00","id":854313,"title":"","content":"Everything risks paradox if you reach too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T19:27:22-07:00","id":854318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=854313#post854313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything risks paradox if you reach too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. But there are multiple ways never even worry about it. My question is why such a heavy hand if you don't need it? <br /> <br /> You targeted him right? So why use the Iron Mask when the Velvet Gloves or Rope are just as effective and for more safe. I'm curious. Or is everyone Cowl? By the way he did serious upper level magic with the intention of manslaughter at the least and did just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 03-27-2016, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T19:29:24-07:00","id":854320,"title":"","content":"And once something has a paradox pool, its not going away, no matter how hard you try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T19:39:30-07:00","id":854326,"title":"","content":"You will probably risk it due to not wanting to cast in ritual time (1 reach), make it last longer than few seconds (another reach to go from combat turns into narrative time) and probably to cast at sensory range (3rd reach). So you need 2 or 3 reaches to cast it comfortably; that would mean Mind 3 or 4 to have it as a safe spell, which is definitely doable.<br /> Wish i could change &quot;will probably&quot; to &quot;might&quot; but stupid phone wont let me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T20:07:32-07:00","id":854334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=854326#post854326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You will probably risk it due to not wanting to cast in ritual time (1 reach), make it last longer than few seconds (another reach to go from combat turns into narrative time) and probably to cast at sensory range (3rd reach). So you need 2 or 3 reaches to cast it comfortably; that would mean Mind 3 or 4 to have it as a safe spell, which is definitely doable.<br /> Wish i could change &amp;quot;will probably&amp;quot; to &amp;quot;might&amp;quot; but stupid phone wont let me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No question here why you'd go for something within your abilities. My question is if you have access to Mind 5 in a combat situation why go all out if a lower level effect or combined spell within your abilities is safer and just as effective?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T01:55:23-07:00","id":854393,"title":"","content":"You mentioned Inuring yourself to the Breach the Mind Vault and that somehow because it incurs Paradox it generates trust. It doesn't incur Paradox though, it just risks it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T18:05:49-07:00","id":854768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=854393#post854393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mentioned Inuring yourself to the Breach the Mind Vault and that somehow because it incurs Paradox it generates trust. It doesn't incur Paradox though, it just risks it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may have read the spoiler incorrectly but the wording gives me the impression that in exchange for never suffering a chance of wisdom loss you incur automatic paradox. Hmm...can you incur wisdom loss by using an attainment? I've never thought you could so if true the trust I mentioned is the fact that something like Breach the Mind Vault without limitation is a scary thing. At least with it being inured and a spell mages could defend against it far better and be safe in the knowledge that the user can go only so far until the risk is in crazy town territory for everyone involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T19:08:46-07:00","id":854808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm...can you incur wisdom loss by using an attainment?</div> </div> </div> </div> I believe it is explicitly called out in the Legacies spoiler that Attainments are integrated into a Mage's soul to a degree such that they cannot cause a Wisdom breaking point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T04:43:12-07:00","id":854992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=854768#post854768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least with it being inured and a spell mages could defend against it far better and be safe in the knowledge that the user can go only so far until the risk is in crazy town territory for everyone involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages can defend against attainments too, they're just not capable of Counterspelling them directly. I don't know what the rest of your sentence means.<br /> <br /> Anyways, yeah Inured spells only risk Paradox they don't incur it and attainments never risk Wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T07:46:59-08:00","id":1054749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=835063#post835063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make impossible photos. Then state that YES, THIS PHOTO IS UNTAMPERED WITH IN ANY WAY. I MADE IT WITH MY OWN CAMERA, AND IT CAPTURED A REAL THING. NO PHOTOSHOP OR OTHER TRICKERY INCLUDED. Which, of course, can boost her prestige as a photographer, but also allows for a very, very horrible perversion that might evolve from her guardian mask:<br /> &quot;This is a picture of your dead body. I took it myself and there was no tampering included with the photo, it really is real. This is your blood, and this is your bone; I took them out with my tools. [insert a lot of descriptions that confirm reality of different wounds, different icky details, and their source] This photo is real and it really captures a scene where I mercilessly killed you. &quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Wisdom saved? Err... but you just destroyed someones soul.<br /> <br /> Pag 98 The origin and destination of souls remains a Mystery even to the Awakened \u2014 they appear at birth and vanish completely at the moment of death.<br /> And then there'1s the spell:<br /> Deny the Reaper (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)}<br /> No matter how long the subject has been dead, minutes or hours, the person\u2019s soul has already moved on, and the subject immediately suffers soul loss. When the spell\u2019s Duration ends, the subject dies again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T08:06:42-08:00","id":1054752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1054749#post1054749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wisdom saved? Err... but you just destroyed someones soul.<br /> <br /> Pag 98 The origin and destination of souls remains a Mystery even to the Awakened \u2014 they appear at birth and vanish completely at the moment of death.<br /> And then there'1s the spell:<br /> Deny the Reaper (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)}<br /> No matter how long the subject has been dead, minutes or hours, the person\u2019s soul has already moved on, and the subject immediately suffers soul loss. When the spell\u2019s Duration ends, the subject dies again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If a person dies in front of you, and you hop back in time, you're going back to before they're dead and may be able to prevent it. They don't just auto-die again because changes made to the past are lasting. Time travel provides a superior version of resurrection than Death does because of the nature of time travel, but it will sometimes have other consequences as well because you screwed with causality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T11:22:11-08:00","id":1054880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank#post831840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes Mage a Monster in your eyes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Blatant disregard for everything that is not mage; refusal even to try and justify your actions by something other than &quot;I want it, so it will be so, and if you don't agree, then suffer the consequences&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T19:41:17-08:00","id":1055509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1054880#post1054880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blatant disregard for everything that is not mage; refusal even to try and justify your actions by something other than &quot;I want it, so it will be so, and if you don't agree, then suffer the consequences&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bExactly. And it rocks and really so easy if you just plan for even a day or so. Unlike WHW if I were a mage I would up my gnosis as fast as possible with my favored Arcana and pick a legacy to get another Arcanum I like as favored quickly as possible. Then start trading rotes for all sorts of favors, teaching, and other rotes. In really useful Arcanum like Fate, Time, Mind, Space, Life, Forces, Prime or Matter depending on what you don't have as favored or above 2-3 dots.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt didn't work as well in Mage the Ascension but it definitely made a huge difference in going for raw power and massive skill in a couple straightforward spheres and 2-3 dots in the support spheres like Entropy/Prime/Correspondence. Mage the Awakening makes it easier in some ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 02-26-2017, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T05:15:13-08:00","id":1055598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank#post831840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- What makes Mage a Monster in your eyes?<br /> - Do you have any interesting examples of it? Double points for examples that come from actual play, and especially from player characters<br /> - What abilities, Arcanas, merits, and other gameplay mechanics do you feel make or could make Mages interesting Monsters?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Obsessions and Nimbus bleed. Paradox should be in there as well; emphasis on the word should; it generally just limits how much Reach an indivudal mage will put into any given spell, in my experience. Never had things reach the point where we were releasing dox instead of containing.<br /> <br /> 2) See below.<br /> <br /> 3) Obsessions and Paradox need better teeth. Mage goes out of the way to make any sort of drawback and just makes everything into a benefit if you happen to engage in it. Obsession should be more than an aspiration, it should be something mages have difficulty turning away from. It should have the same influence that frenzy or death rage do for wolves and vamps, or fear of exposure does in changeling. <br /> <br /> <br /> So, lets begin. Nimbus. My players, new to 2e, didn't really make much out of Nimbus. They kind of mixed in their mundane and magical lives. They generally chose Nimbus that would be most beneficial during combat or other similar situations. And... they began to use magic in their everyday lives. The area around the PCs very steadily became a living hell as people took penalties to their Resolve and Composure and their perception ability. Misunderstandings and hair trigger tempers and lashing out eveywhere. It was a disaster as people became selfish and driven to extremes. No one had self control. Not even the PCs themselves as they infected each other with their Nimbuses (nimbi?). Eventually I had the Guardians step in and put a cell in place to clean up the mess, and some serious scoldings for the PCs. It was a learning curve to realize that even subtle magics around humanity leads to bad things. By all rights, I should have also had a Wisdom breaking point here, but since everyone was properly horrified ICly and realized their ignorance, I felt it was unnecessary.<br /> <br /> I make extensive use of the Astral in my games, including for joining Legacies and sharing Libraries among people. I've actually had mages &quot;save&quot; and expand the Library of Alexandria (or, at least the Astral version of it). We're actually dealing with going into the Underwolrd and recovering &quot;dead&quot; knowlege and copying it to here. There's a whole storyhook for mages in the Book of the Dead on that. Anyways, during a particular trip to get some books by sneaking past some antagonistic Keroberus and getting some books, I arranged for a few mages to waylay the group for their own copies. Nimbus flairs spread, and... everyone basically crippled themsleves in that fight, both enemies and allies. The battle tide basically ended with an enemy Mastigos pulling the book copies into their own hand and teleporting away. With all the Tilts lying thick as curses, no one could actually notice when the books were stolen, or didn't for a long while. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Obsessions are where the fun is at. I'm not above mixing the Obsession Condition with the Obsession mage trait at times. I found that the players weren't too strongly invested in Obsessions, and easily walked away from them without penalty. So, I added a bit of a stick that worried at the characters at times. It gaves them a bit of stronger focus in my game. Anyways, four players, each of whom I assigned a different &quot;antagonist&quot; - a Seer, a Banisher, an Acamoth and a Tremere, all around the central Mystery of being stuck in a non-existant-yet-still-somehow-here city. <br /> <br /> In one particular case, the group Acanthus had an Obsession with the boundry between Luck and Destiny. So, not realizing that the line was an Exarch, I actually had a Seer walk up to our Acanthus and start dangling some information in front of her. She, knowing it for the trap it was, refused. I then proceeded to roll some dice behind a screen, and (I admit to lying here) claimed the Seer used some Social merits to get an exceptional success on a roll. She could refuse, of coures... but she became Obsessed with the information in the back of her mind. The group discussed Mind magic surgery to &quot;purge&quot; each other's emotions in this case. I think they only reason they didn't is because I started checking books with a big grin on my face. My playgroup does NOT like it when I start checking books mid-game; they know I'm planning something. A bit meta-game-y, perhaps, but it got home the point; relying on mind magic for this kind of thing is bad, m'kay? Anyways, Baba Yaga got tired of being penalized on all the rolls, and eventually snapped, coming up with a plan for the information without endangering herself. Turns out that Destiny is part of the Lie and is artificially imposed by magical beings working their will to force people to do stuff. And, for her trouble, not only did the player get double the beats and some mana, but she also got a free grimoire out of the deal with some custom rotes in it for sensing how destiny was being manipulated. I had an entire temptation-plot going on for joining the Seers, but the game kind of imploded after a bit due to real life concerns. <br /> <br /> <br /> Another situation, same game. Our group Obrimos wanted to go all Choir of Hasmallim. Obsession with <i>fighting</i> the Abyss is very quickly turned to fighting fire with fire. Learning that mages can taint their magic or control paradox was something that Michael learned early on. I even dropped a grimoire for new Scelesti into his lap. It had a few tainted rotes in it, and, for each one he studied, he figured out how to reverse engineer scelsti techniques. Of course, currently he wasn't Scelesti, but he could easily become one now if he desired. And then... during a plot with some scelesti (with the one Scelseti legacy from Summoners), I kept dropping little situations that he could more easily get out of by taking control of the deliberately released paradox effects. He'd be -more- effective fighting fire with fire. Finally got him to do it once before the scelesti ran away. Rewarded him with some arcane xp and a free new pseudo-Obsession related to tainting spells (this replaced the 1e Addiction effect). The player was -very- tempted to cast tainted spells now as a free source of arcane xp and mana. <br /> <br /> <br /> Obsessions, in my opinion, should drive mages to one of the antagonist factions. Seer, Banisher, Scelesti, Reaper, Lich or Mad. They're all examples of what happens when a mage lets his Obsessions with Mysteries cloud his judgement. So, that's what I did with them. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T08:28:28-08:00","id":1055657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055598#post1055598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Obsessions and Paradox need better teeth. Mage goes out of the way to make any sort of drawback and just makes everything into a benefit if you happen to engage in it. Obsession should be more than an aspiration, it should be something mages have difficulty turning away from. It should have the same influence that frenzy or death rage do for wolves and vamps, or fear of exposure does in changeling</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree wholeheartedly with this. As they are, Obsessions are treated as magical Aspirations, while mechanically that's what they are. And Paradox <i>seems </i>like it's going to get you sometimes, for instance with the Abyss seeping into your Pattern and affecting all your spells, but you can get rid of it by scouring for one Lethal.<br /> <br /> A lot of people focus on the power, but that's just the tool. Tweaking Obsessions and Paradox, I think, are the key to playing up consequences and making them a more significant part of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-27-2017, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T08:37:11-08:00","id":1055662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055657#post1055657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but you can get rid of it by scouring for one Lethal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll just leave <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1029550-what-happens-when-a-paradox-condition-lapses?p=1029936#post1029936\">this</a> here again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T09:26:54-08:00","id":1055681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055657#post1055657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of people focus on the power, but that's just the tool. Tweaking Obsessions and Paradox, I think, are the key to playing up consequences and making them a more significant part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or instead of saying the rules don't work as intended start to actually utilize the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T09:44:41-08:00","id":1055685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055662#post1055662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll just leave <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1029550-what-happens-when-a-paradox-condition-lapses?p=1029936#post1029936\">this</a> here again.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point was scouring is the end of it, whether you get a Beat or not is irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055681#post1055681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or instead of saying the rules don't work as intended start to actually utilize the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say that. The rules are working as intended, the intention seems to be a game with great power and little drawback to said power. Obsessions are even described in terms of being 'just like long-term Aspirations,' with the only 'bite' to the idea being a 1-die penalty in rolls to check Wisdom if following said Obsession. And Paradox is not a threat that lingers unless you, for whatever reason, want it to.<br /> <br /> There's just a disparity between what some players want out of the game and what others do. If you believe the game is fine on its own, that's great, but so far your perspective is offering little to the thread other than sarcastic one liners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T09:49:57-08:00","id":1055688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055685#post1055685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point was scouring is the end of it, whether you get a Beat or not is irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>And my point is that it's extremely clear the intent is not that you can just get rid of any Paradox Condition no-muss-no-fuss by using the method that the actual description of the process places <i>after</i> the Condition lapses, or else there's literally no point to the duration chart that steers the incentives toward containment at high-Wisdom/low-Gnosis and releasing at low-Wisdom/high-Gnosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T09:53:30-08:00","id":1055689,"title":"","content":"I don't think a Mage is inherently a monster like (some of) the other splats. There's no &quot;A Beast I Am, Lest A Beast I Become&quot; with Mages. You can, in fact, be a good witch, if you adhere to Wisdom. This is what makes Mage less of a horror game and more of urban fantasy on its own, though the level of horror is generally cosmic horror - what you COULD be, if you let go of all restrictions, plus the existential terror of both The Lie and The Abyss.<br /> <br /> But a Mage certainly CAN become a monster, depending on their obsession and their Wisdom rating. And it's incredibly, incredibly easy to become a monster when you have phenomenal cosmic power. Remember Baron Acton - &quot;Power tends to corrupt, and absolute power corrupts absolutely. Great men are almost always bad men.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T10:51:29-08:00","id":1055712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055685#post1055685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say that. The rules are working as intended, the intention seems to be a game with great power and little drawback to said power. Obsessions are even described in terms of being 'just like long-term Aspirations,' with the only 'bite' to the idea being a 1-die penalty in rolls to check Wisdom if following said Obsession. And Paradox is not a threat that lingers unless you, for whatever reason, want it to.<br /> <br /> There's just a disparity between what some players want out of the game and what others do. If you believe the game is fine on its own, that's great, but so far your perspective is offering little to the thread other than sarcastic one liners.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're saying that Paradox and Obsession need to be tweaked then you are saying that. Anyway, the obvious downside to not using your Obsessions are power disparity and the loss of a die when using Scrutiny on an Obsession related subject and also you lose the chance to use Obsession to affect Social Maneuvering. Basically, sure, you can not use it but you're not doing yourself any favors.<br /> <br /> Thinking of Paradox as an existential threat is counter to the game's themes anyway. That's just an immediate consequence of carelessness. The setting encourages Mages to think that reality hates them, and Paradox is a passive reactionary aspect of that. It's kind of pointless to complain about it being anything else when you're supposed to be going after them with the entirety of the rest of reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T13:52:53-08:00","id":1055768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055689#post1055689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think a Mage is inherently a monster like (some of) the other splats. There's no &quot;A Beast I Am, Lest A Beast I Become&quot; with Mages. You can, in fact, be a good witch, if you adhere to Wisdom. This is what makes Mage less of a horror game and more of urban fantasy on its own, though the level of horror is generally cosmic horror - what you COULD be, if you let go of all restrictions, plus the existential terror of both The Lie and The Abyss.<br /> <br /> But a Mage certainly CAN become a monster, depending on their obsession and their Wisdom rating. And it's incredibly, incredibly easy to become a monster when you have phenomenal cosmic power. Remember Baron Acton - &quot;Power tends to corrupt, and absolute power corrupts absolutely. Great men are almost always bad men.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>But by that logic, werewolves can also be 'good' as long as they hunt things humans would be ok with, act in a manner coinciding with your definition of good, and avoid triggers/load up on things/hang out with people who can help them to control Death Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 02-27-2017, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T14:03:29-08:00","id":1055774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055681#post1055681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or instead of saying the rules don't work as intended start to actually utilize the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm going to flatly disagree with this. Because, even if as an ST I make every NPC being a power abuser monster, that means that we will have PCs that... aren't monsters. I am firmly of the opinion that every supernatural, irregardless of individual details, should have mechanics that reflect their monstrous nature. If there's no mechanics, then there's nothing to hold PCs to any kind of &quot;monster&quot; nature. There's nothing to force a pc to act like a jerkwad, and if that's what makes mages monsters, then it kind of fails for all mages. Some, sure. You want to argue the majority, sure, I don't care about that. But you can't say every mage.<br /> <br /> Honestly, there's very good reasons why so many people feel that mages aren't monsters despite the setting premisis and outright Word of God on the matter. Telling people to &quot;utilize the setting&quot; is not going to fix it. Not only because we'll have individuals who aren't acting the way the setting demands, but it does nothing to help people that utilize non-standard settings, like myself. I don't want someone to just tell me mages are monsters because they abuse power, then insist that my non-abusive Enlightened magus is still a monster when she engages in none of the abusive attitudes. My first 2e mage was a doctor, and her first Obsession was to gain Wisdom. My first goal was to aim right for Wisdom 8. She had no interest in doing crazy experiments on people, or do torture. How is she a monster?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-27-2017, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T14:05:10-08:00","id":1055776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055768#post1055768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But by that logic, werewolves can also be 'good' as long as they hunt things humans would be ok with, act in a manner coinciding with your definition of good, and avoid triggers/load up on things/hang out with people who can help them to/of control Death Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure about that, just because if a Werewolf becomes too close to Flesh, they can lose their ability to shift, and basically stop being &quot;Werewolves.&quot; In order to stay a Werewolf, you need to split your time between being Flesh and Spirit. And a Werewolf defending the world of Flesh from the Spirit is a monster to the Spirit, and a Werewolf defending the world of Shadow from the Flesh is a monster to the Flesh. In that way, I think, Werewolf has its own &quot;A Beast I Am, Lest A Beast I Become&quot; in that it is &quot;A Beast I Am, Lest I Forget Who I Am.&quot; Being part Spirit and part Flesh is WHAT YOU ARE. You weren't turned into a Werewolf, it's what you've always been. If you reject that, you will lose yourself. You're going to have to be a monster sometimes.<br /> <br /> Obviously this is THE core theme of Vampire. Promethean monstrosity is enforced by the Disquiet. They don't have to be 'bad people,' but everybody looks at them and sees a big old freak. They can never just be regular people because they're not. Unless they achieve the New Dawn. Changelings, likewise, don't have to be monsters, but there is sort of &quot;A Beast I Am Lest A Beast I Become&quot; in that they build their freeholds and courts and absorb glamour and do their faerie magic to put themselves in a position to stay safe from the Fae. They have to be weird, strange, otherworldly creatures and not just regular humans because otherwise the literal Big Bad Wolf is going to come and eat them. Sin-Eaters have ghosts in their heads that want to do terrible, alien things because they are terrible and alien. A Sin-Eater could ignore these urges, of course, but it's kind of a dick move given that the ghost brought you back to life and all.<br /> <br /> Mages are the only ones who have a choice to be good and moral and never have to do anything that humans would deem monstrous. But there's a huge potential to become a monster when you have the powers of a God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T15:01:38-08:00","id":1055810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055774#post1055774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, there's very good reasons why so many people feel that mages aren't monsters despite the setting premisis and outright Word of God on the matter. Telling people to &quot;utilize the setting&quot; is not going to fix it. Not only because we'll have individuals who aren't acting the way the setting demands, but it does nothing to help people that utilize non-standard settings, like myself. I don't want someone to just tell me mages are monsters because they abuse power, then insist that my non-abusive Enlightened magus is still a monster when she engages in none of the abusive attitudes. My first 2e mage was a doctor, and her first Obsession was to gain Wisdom. My first goal was to aim right for Wisdom 8. She had no interest in doing crazy experiments on people, or do torture. How is she a monster?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's my two cents. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Mages are monsters because that level of power is inherently abusive.<br /> The monstrosity of Mages is not in the mean and intentionally abusive ways they use their power, but in the abuse that is done by even the most well-intentioned of choices. (easier if they're also mean and intentionally abusive)<br /> Your non-abusive Enlightened magus might try not to engage in abusive attitudes, but how does she make peace between her newly discovered power and her drives as a doctor? You don't become a doc because you were a bit bored and took a course, it takes years of dedicated study, and this takes drive. And now you learn a lot of it was a Lie? (see the 'The World is a Lie' text in the book)<br /> What is this drive? Is it the clichee 'I want to help people?' or something a bit different? Does she use magic to heal the sick? If not, why not? How mean. If yes, why just those? Don't others deserve the same help? Could you wipe out diseases on a global scale? Could you enhance people's immune systems on that scale?<br /> <br /> And for any of those questions that is answered with &quot;magic time now!,&quot; what are the consequences of this? I don't even mean for Wisdom if they're well thought-out. Magic is very nice for short-term(even if that is years) and specific problems. And easily neglects long-term effects and even just side-effects. You wipe out a disease cca 15% of humanity is at risk of, does the lack of this disease open a place to a different one, or perhaps result in a lack of immunity to something unexpected? You boost a town's resistance to disease and they're shiny and healthy, you even make it hereditary ... are they now carriers of diseases they are unaffected by, or cause pathogens to mutate to overcome this resistance?<br /> How about encountering an illness that is of magical origin? MYSTERY!<br /> A grand undertaking - because why wouldn't you with that kind of power, how selfish can you be to just do nothing - carries grand risks. Monstrous risks.<br /> <br /> Utilising the setting is not &quot;just make every NPC an asshat because that's the way to go for horror.&quot; It's going with the themes and moods of the game you've chosen to play. Try reading the &quot;Addicted To Mysteries&quot; text again, I find it quite inspiring for the thematic consistency and mood of the game.<br /> <br /> Becoming more Wise is a laudable aspiration. But doesn't she use magic? The tools that are given, as it were? No interacting with the Wisdom mechanic outside the &quot;I am Wise, and shall be more so?&quot; Do Obsessions really need to have a punishment mechanic for them to be played as intended?<br /> <br /> Stream of thought over. Hope some of it was of some use <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Final thought: A Beast I Am Because I Am The Seed Of A Cosmic Horror And Virtually Nothing Can Stand Before My Will <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11842,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","user":"Aeryes","date":".  Adding a final thought 02-27-2017, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T15:07:15-08:00","id":1055814,"title":"","content":"@MCN Saying that you should use the setting is a valid argument. Mages are the monsters of genie wishes, monkey paws and unintended consequences an ST should be all kinds of alert for those opportunities while trying not to cross the line into being a jerk. The fact that their power is inherently easy for them to use is part of the setting's horror because it also means it's ripe for abuse. How does having Wisdom as an Obsession render you a monster? It means you'll be experimenting with what's Wise, Mages don't instinctively know and Wisdom is mutable. I don't really want to get into the whole Wisdom debate again because it's been done to death, but I'm firmly in the camp that because it's not a set in stone standard for any Mage it must not be about being good. Not being good seems to be how people define being a monster. That doesn't require mechanics to force people to be &quot;bad&quot; though. Hell, Mages are -more- culpable for their moral failings because they could choose not to indulge them. If you play a saint and that makes you feel good, then great, but as the ST I'd provide plenty of counter-examples and I'd also throw in the temptation to stray off the path of your indignant moral righteousness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T15:07:16-08:00","id":1055815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055776#post1055776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not so sure about that, just because if a Werewolf becomes too close to Flesh, they can lose their ability to shift, and basically stop being &quot;Werewolves.&quot; In order to stay a Werewolf, you need to split your time between being Flesh and Spirit. And a Werewolf defending the world of Flesh from the Spirit is a monster to the Spirit, and a Werewolf defending the world of Shadow from the Flesh is a monster to the Flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really how it works. Hunting threats to humanity wouldn't make you any more Flesh, it's likely to put you more Spirit as you're fulfilling the spirit of the hunt part of yourself.<br /> <br /> And a werewolf who goes fully Flesh, Harmony 10, doesn't quite cease to be a werewolf. The just become a werewolf at moments they cannot control and only go Death Rage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In that way, I think, Werewolf has its own &quot;A Beast I Am, Lest A Beast I Become&quot; in that it is &quot;A Beast I Am, Lest I Forget Who I Am.&quot; Being part Spirit and part Flesh is WHAT YOU ARE. You weren't turned into a Werewolf, it's what you've always been. If you reject that, you will lose yourself. You're going to have to be a monster sometimes. </div> </div> </div>Rejecting the Spirit or Flesh side, or clinging too closely to one, is where you have problems. And one shouldn't associate Flesh with humanity, it's not about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-27-2017, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T15:16:39-08:00","id":1055822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055815#post1055815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not really how it works. Hunting threats to humanity wouldn't make you any more Flesh, it's likely to put you more Spirit as you're fulfilling the spirit of the hunt part of yourself.<br /> <br /> Rejecting the Spirit or Flesh side, or clinging too closely to one, is where you have problems. And one shouldn't associate Flesh with humanity, it's not about that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll be the first to admit, I pulled most of that out of my rear end. I'm in the PROCESS of reading Werewolf 2nd edition, so this is from the perspective of someone who kinda sorta gets the themes of the games from a rough draft reading of the first 100 pages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T15:16:47-08:00","id":1055823,"title":"","content":"Mages are inherently &quot;World Inside the Gourd&quot; style-monsters, who's essence extends beyond themselves and feedbacks into them, thus skewing their perspective into something alien, who eventually commit to self-memetic-mutation into the Nightmare-Named-Myself (&quot;The demon that comes when people call its name&quot;, heh). Even the highest-Wisdom Mage is a creature whose essential nature is so warped it can no longer be called human.<br /> <br /> This weird desire to divorce Mages from their magic in the declaration of their being is probably the root of the argument, and to treat the two as seperate is not only false, but the failing that ensures that any who become such monsters invariably will become nightmares.<br /> <br /> Mages are their magic, always. Magic is not human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-27-2017, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T16:29:55-08:00","id":1055862,"title":"","content":"Mages are Monsters when they act without regards to Wisdom.<br /> But more than that, Mages are Monsters when they take various options which strike certain actions from being Acts of Hubris.<br /> <br /> Guardians who commit the most horrifying crimes, hiding behind their Masques.<br /> Legacies who make rampant use of Attainments in morally deplorable manners, or have Attainments which by their nature are horrifying.<br /> Anyone who Inures a spell they know is morally heinous, so that they can keep doing it anyway and defer responsibility for their actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T16:34:39-08:00","id":1055865,"title":"","content":"A mage with high Wisdom is a monster that is in control of itself.<br /> <br /> A mage with low Wisdom is a monster that is not in control of itself.<br /> <br /> There's a fundamental reality to the being that must be acknowledged before Wisdom even matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T17:06:04-08:00","id":1055885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055822#post1055822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be the first to admit, I pulled most of that out of my rear end. I'm in the PROCESS of reading Werewolf 2nd edition, so this is from the perspective of someone who kinda sorta gets the themes of the games from a rough draft reading of the first 100 pages.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want, I have a crappy, aborted write-up about the monstrosity of Uratha that ignores the whole &quot;zomg body horror i am a wolf guys&quot; angle. It's just sitting around in my GDrive right now gathering digital dust.<br /> <br /> One of the hard things about CofD monstrosity is that it requires some distance between player and character in order to be horrified by the character's experience. It doesn't really work for people who look at monsters and go, &quot;Ooh, that's my wet dream of wish fulfillment,&quot; which makes it something of a hard sell for a lot of RPG players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T17:41:47-08:00","id":1055908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055865#post1055865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mage with high Wisdom is a monster that is in control of itself.<br /> <br /> A mage with low Wisdom is a monster that is not in control of itself.<br /> <br /> There's a fundamental reality to the being that must be acknowledged before Wisdom even matters.</div> </div> </div> </div> What exactly makes someone or something a Monster?<br /> <br /> Because if a Mage isn't hurting people, does nice things, and has a high wisdom, calling them Monsters is a hard sell, especially to anyone coming from a D&amp;D background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T17:55:21-08:00","id":1055916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055908#post1055908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly makes someone or something a Monster?<br /> <br /> Because if a Mage isn't hurting people, does nice things, and has a high wisdom, calling them Monsters is a hard sell, especially to anyone coming from a D&amp;D background.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that despite any lies they tell themselves they are not part of the human experience anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T19:54:34-08:00","id":1055957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055916#post1055916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact that despite any lies they tell themselves they are not part of the human experience anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if 'the human experience' was just a Lie dreamed up by some Evil Wizard Symbols to keep you docile and enslaved, and now you're awake, and you know kung fu, and you're hanging around with this cool chick and a bald black guy, are you still a monster, or are you a hero?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T20:16:07-08:00","id":1055959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055957#post1055957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But if 'the human experience' was just a Lie dreamed up by some Evil Wizard Symbols to keep you docile and enslaved, and now you're awake, and you know kung fu, and you're hanging around with this cool chick and a bald black guy, are you still a monster, or are you a hero?</div> </div> </div> </div>A common end goal among your species is trying to splat yourself against the cave paintings that inform the universe and survive. Undergoing your equivalent of normal people's world-shaking uncomfortable personal revelations on a regular basis will turn you into a reckless asshole rather than a nervous wreck. The burning flame of your mystery addiction attempts to feed your friends and loved ones to itself unless you properly label your Wizard Time and sort things that aren't magic into the pile that's not that one. The downbeat of chasing your highs brings tendrils of an un-being wearing the skin of an antediluvian creator-god into your municipality if you don't coat your spells in raw Truth-As-She-Is-Manifested-On-Earth, make the appropriate sacrifices, and play the right kind of dress-up.<br /> <br /> We call that a monster most days of the week, particularly when the kung fu turns your organs into a flesh-intruder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T20:45:06-08:00","id":1055968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055957#post1055957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if 'the human experience' was just a Lie dreamed up by some Evil Wizard Symbols to keep you docile and enslaved, and now you're awake, and you know kung fu, and you're hanging around with this cool chick and a bald black guy, are you still a monster, or are you a hero?</div> </div> </div> </div>The default state of mortals (Before the Fall) is to be a Sleepwalker. Those who cross beyond that by whichever route can't truly be considered human. You might feel like or aspire to be a hero, but you aren't. You're just as inhuman as the next monster. Mages just have the luxury of being able to lie to themselves more convincingly about it. Considering the devs call John Constantine a high Wisdom Mage...you'll be lucky if everyone you care about only ends up dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T21:12:53-08:00","id":1055977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055957#post1055957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But if 'the human experience' was just a Lie dreamed up by some Evil Wizard Symbols to keep you docile and enslaved, and now you're awake, and you know kung fu, and you're hanging around with this cool chick and a bald black guy, are you still a monster, or are you a hero?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're assuming heroes aren't monsters.<br /> <br /> That's a fallacy.<br /> <br /> You're also assuming that just because you are awake, know kung fu, and hang out with a cool chick and bald black guy, you're a hero.<br /> <br /> That's a fallacy.<br /> <br /> You're also assuming that a hero is the best or most desirable thing you can want to be in this world.<br /> <br /> That's a fallacy.<br /> <br /> These are fallacies that transform monsters(read aliens) into monsters(read nightmares). Abandon preconceptions in this world, lest you think the mysteries must be answered instead of transformed into and enlightenment and equanimity be barred from you forever, leaving you trapped in the prison of your self.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T21:53:12-08:00","id":1055989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055774#post1055774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm going to flatly disagree with this. Because, even if as an ST I make every NPC being a power abuser monster, that means that we will have PCs that... aren't monsters. I am firmly of the opinion that every supernatural, irregardless of individual details, should have mechanics that reflect their monstrous nature. If there's no mechanics, then there's nothing to hold PCs to any kind of &quot;monster&quot; nature. There's nothing to force a pc to act like a jerkwad, and if that's what makes mages monsters, then it kind of fails for all mages. Some, sure. You want to argue the majority, sure, I don't care about that. But you can't say every mage.<br /> <br /> Honestly, there's very good reasons why so many people feel that mages aren't monsters despite the setting premisis and outright Word of God on the matter. Telling people to &quot;utilize the setting&quot; is not going to fix it. Not only because we'll have individuals who aren't acting the way the setting demands, but it does nothing to help people that utilize non-standard settings, like myself. I don't want someone to just tell me mages are monsters because they abuse power, then insist that my non-abusive Enlightened magus is still a monster when she engages in none of the abusive attitudes. My first 2e mage was a doctor, and her first Obsession was to gain Wisdom. My first goal was to aim right for Wisdom 8. She had no interest in doing crazy experiments on people, or do torture. How is she a monster?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou answered your individual issue about Mages being assholes because they are in fact damn powerful without any help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T23:29:38-08:00","id":1056001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055774#post1055774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want someone to just tell me mages are monsters because they abuse power, then insist that my non-abusive Enlightened magus is still a monster when she engages in none of the abusive attitudes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The abusive attitudes are partially enforced through the fact that failing a breaking point roll gives you Conditions that render it impossible for a Gnosis 1-2 character to pursue higher Wisdom until they are discharged (when discharging those Conditions de facto involves more risks to your Wisdom). Mages who lose Wisdom become selfish and careless and get pips of the resource that lets them buy Wisdom for things as simple as casting in front of Sleepers \u2014 and start getting incentivized to inure spells and let Paradox become more of an issue than Wisdom loss, which in turn means they've either become more Mana-dependent or locked off a spell for special occasions.<br /> <br /> For that matter, having the necessary Obsession to cultivate Wisdom inherently raises the risk in every Act of Hubris you engage with, and it takes an entire story of fruit-bearing actual-work enlightenment-seeking to get the opportunity to spend those ten Arcane Beats that you will almost certainly earn faster if you court degeneration to woo Sophia. If you feel confident making that many unboostable two-dice rolls at the risk of losing more Wisdom, your secure place in the cosmos could well be one that you got to by leaving a trail of devastation in your wake, and you'll be a lot better off than the folks who're just going cold-turkey.<br /> <br /> Yes, low-Tolerance-high-Integrity supernatural beings like most starting characters are going to be able to act in a manner acceptable to mortal society without much distress. This is not a new phenomenon \u2014 it's an entire easily-viable playstyle in Demon, for instance \u2014 and it changes very little about the all-consuming lore-hunger squatting at the center of your web of occult sympathies waiting to poison your life and your home if you break character with the wrong people while pretending not to be carrying one of the most invasive investigative implements conceivable by human thought.<br /> <br /> As a point of curiosity, what's the fuller context of the enlightened doctor's quest for Wisdom?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T00:05:16-08:00","id":1056004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055957#post1055957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But if 'the human experience' was just a Lie dreamed up by some Evil Wizard Symbols to keep you docile and enslaved, and now you're awake, and you know kung fu, and you're hanging around with this cool chick and a bald black guy, are you still a monster, or are you a hero?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know you're trying to do Neo, but you're really doing Anakin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T02:55:31-08:00","id":1056029,"title":"","content":"To me, even a high-Wisdom mage is still a monster the same way Paarthurnax is still a dragon, despite all the self-discipline both practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T03:26:01-08:00","id":1056039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055977#post1055977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are fallacies that transform monsters(read aliens) into monsters(read nightmares).</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be a language thing and I might be alone in this, but I think that those who can see mages as not being monsters also don't see alien/inhuman beings as inherently a monster. For me a monster has to do (or set out to do) something evil or otherwise do harm. A mage that is capable of retaining high Wisdom and not fuck up the lives of others would hardly be a monster by that definition.<br /> So I think this thread really needs a solid definition for monsters before people can meaningfully discuss whether or not mages fulfil that definition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T03:48:32-08:00","id":1056043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1056039#post1056039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I think this thread really needs a solid definition for monsters before people can meaningfully discuss whether or not mages fulfil that definition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bearing in mind that this is a necroed thread, the last two pages have been pretty much exactly what WHW asked people not to do.<br /> <br /> I agree though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T04:03:51-08:00","id":1056047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055810#post1055810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages are monsters because that level of power is inherently abusive.<br /> The monstrosity of Mages is not in the mean and intentionally abusive ways they use their power, but in the abuse that is done by even the most well-intentioned of choices. (easier if they're also mean and intentionally abusive)<br /> Your non-abusive Enlightened magus might try not to engage in abusive attitudes, but how does she make peace between her newly discovered power and her drives as a doctor? You don't become a doc because you were a bit bored and took a course, it takes years of dedicated study, and this takes drive. And now you learn a lot of it was a Lie? (see the 'The World is a Lie' text in the book)<br /> What is this drive? Is it the clichee 'I want to help people?' or something a bit different? Does she use magic to heal the sick? If not, why not? How mean. If yes, why just those? Don't others deserve the same help? Could you wipe out diseases on a global scale? Could you enhance people's immune systems on that scale?</div> </div> </div> </div> .... Yeah, no. First of all, that's not how abuse actually works. Secondly, no, it wasn't a Lie. That sidebar actually refers to the Exarchs and Seers ruling the world, and suggests the Pentacle (and thus the PCs) is at war with them. Not that Sleeper Science is wrong. In fact, for someone who's also a part of Free Council who believes that science is an echo of seeking Supernal Truth? Frankly, I don't see my PC having any qualms with making peace between &quot;newly discovered power&quot; and being a doctor. She had qualms about the people close to her being subject to Long Term Nimbus (thus the Wisdom). But the power itself? Not really.<br /> <br /> Secondly, choosing to not to help people is not a &quot;monstrous choice.&quot; There's fairly well established ethics in the medical community about responcibility to patients as well as to the self. That's why the Wisdom - the understanding when its best to apply the balance of the personal life and the duties as a doctor and the life as a mage. Its knowing that experimenting on living people is kidn of a bad, immoral thing that shouldn't be done. Its knowing that there are times when casting magic shouldn't be done. <br /> <br /> Third, &quot;wanting to help people&quot; is not a cliche. I went into social services because I want to help people in real life. Its called &quot;this actually happens with a lot of frequency.&quot; <br /> <br /> I feel like you're trying to tell me that my character is going to absolutely make &quot;wrong choices&quot; because she's a mage. That's kind of circular reasoning. Mages are monsters because they make wrong choices, and they make wrong choices because they're monstrous mages. Everything you're suggesting is a choice. And, you know what? Even when picking between bad choices, that doesn't make someone inherantly a monster. It just makes them a flawed human with others being judgemental. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do Obsessions really need to have a punishment mechanic for them to be played as intended? </div> </div> </div> No. Does it make them more effective and evocative? I find that to be a yes.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055814#post1055814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@MCN Saying that you should use the setting is a valid argument.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, as far as I'm concerned, its a crap argument. I feel that its basically telling me how to run my game. That's never a good argument. If I want to run a neolithic Mage game, with an effectively isolated mage cabal / circle of PCs, then I should and still have the PCs feel like a monster. Paradox, Nimbus and Obsessions give me the tools for that. Or, at least, they should. Without them? *shakes head sadly*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fact that their power is inherently easy for them to use is part of the setting's horror because it also means it's ripe for abuse. </div> </div> </div> Ripe for abuse does not equal actual abused. That's nothing more than the &quot;power corrupts&quot; line that has been scientifically proven false and is not part of Mage 2e by default. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does having Wisdom as an Obsession render you a monster? It means you'll be experimenting with what's Wise, </div> </div> </div> No... it means you'll be studying what is Wise. Obsession does not equate to experimentation in every situation. It can, but its not a given. There are many ways of achiving an Obsession.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not being good seems to be how people define being a monster. </div> </div> </div> No, if I used that definition, then Prometheans and Changelings wouldn't be monsters. I don't even use &quot;anti-social behaviors.&quot; I personally go with &quot;evoking moods of fear and disgust/rejection.&quot; YMMV.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That doesn't require mechanics to force people to be &quot;bad&quot; though. That makes you feel good, then great, but as the ST I'd provide plenty of counter-examples and I'd also throw in the temptation to stray off the path of your indignant moral righteousness. </div> </div> </div> You're saying that I can play a mage that's not a monster? See, that's exactly why I think it should be mechanics that make one a monster. Every single Awakened, without exception, should be a monster. All vampires are monsters. All werewolves are monsters. All Prometheans and changelings and Unchained and Begotten are monsters. The same should hold true with Awakened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055916#post1055916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that despite any lies they tell themselves they are not part of the human experience anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not human does not equal monster. I am firmly of the opinion that you can have beings that aren't part of the human experience and aren't monsters, even in the CofD. It tends to not come up, because of this being a game about playing monsters, but that doesn't mean we're dealing with an absolute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T05:35:10-08:00","id":1056067,"title":"","content":"You can't just study, Mage is pretty clear that the Awakened condition has to be experienced to gain understanding in its different facets, Wisdom included.<br /> <br /> I'm saying you might be able to pull off the saint, but I'd use your position as such to highlight the flaws of the Awakened in general. Your personal success wouldn't make Mages as a whole any less monstrous. As for monstrosity being fear and disgust, just what do you think Dissonance is? Sure, it might be Abyssaly influenced, but the fact is that you're an aberration that harms others by expressing your own nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T06:48:30-08:00","id":1056087,"title":"","content":"Just a reminder in the thread that four of the six playable Orders in the core have as tenets that aren't really debated:<br /> <br /> -That anyone who isn't a wizard should absolutely led without question by their wizard masters (who are doing it for their own good, honest).<br /> -That Sleepers should not be allowed near secret knowledge and that, by their inability to Awaken, they've proven themselves unworthy of access to the real truths of the world.<br /> -What the other guy said, but going so far as to spread outright misinformation and lies to try and keep them from Awakening.<br /> -Using your wizardly powers to tilt a conflict to match your personal vision is A-Okay.<br /> <br /> And that's without pointing out that of the two remaining, one looked at Gnosticism and thought the Demiurge was the good guy, and the other is only hard to say anything bad about because there's <i>so little to them</i>; the Libertines are like a sewing circle for people who disagree with Atlantean dogma and think that democracy is real neato, but they still maintain the Veil and manipulate Sleeper societies.<br /> <br /> Wizards don't need in-built features to be monstrous; just give a chimpanzee a box of hand grenades and nature sorts itself out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T09:06:04-08:00","id":1056136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1056087#post1056087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a reminder in the thread that four of the six playable Orders in the core have as tenets that aren't really debated:<br /> <br /> -That anyone who isn't a wizard should absolutely led without question by their wizard masters (who are doing it for their own good, honest).<br /> -That Sleepers should not be allowed near secret knowledge and that, by their inability to Awaken, they've proven themselves unworthy of access to the real truths of the world.<br /> -What the other guy said, but going so far as to spread outright misinformation and lies to try and keep them from Awakening.<br /> -Using your wizardly powers to tilt a conflict to match your personal vision is A-Okay.<br /> <br /> And that's without pointing out that of the two remaining, one looked at Gnosticism and thought the Demiurge was the good guy, and the other is only hard to say anything bad about because there's <i>so little to them</i>; the Libertines are like a sewing circle for people who disagree with Atlantean dogma and think that democracy is real neato, but they still maintain the Veil and manipulate Sleeper societies.<br /> <br /> Wizards don't need in-built features to be monstrous; just give a chimpanzee a box of hand grenades and nature sorts itself out.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Free Council actually aren't little-they consistently make up the second largest orders in any given area as a general rule. The Free Council are fucked up for a couple of reasons(like the others), but if you want a classically easy one, &quot;Destroy the Followers of the Lie&quot; is often super easy to cast as &quot;Destroy anyone who disagrees with us.&quot; It happens fairly often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T09:12:52-08:00","id":1056143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1056039#post1056039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It might be a language thing and I might be alone in this, but I think that those who can see mages as not being monsters also don't see alien/inhuman beings as inherently a monster. For me a monster has to do (or set out to do) something evil or otherwise do harm. A mage that is capable of retaining high Wisdom and not fuck up the lives of others would hardly be a monster by that definition.<br /> So I think this thread really needs a solid definition for monsters before people can meaningfully discuss whether or not mages fulfil that definition.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be why I clarified the two kinds of monsters, aliens and nightmares, trying to very punchily summarize the distinction in phrase use. A lot of people are arguing, rightly, that where all that power leads a mage and their common arcs as reasons why they are a monster, and why a mage that avoids that should not be tarred with that brush.<br /> <br /> I'm not taking that route. My point is that I don't think it's accurate to treat mages as human anymore, that to think of them that way is one of the keys things that leads to the attitudes that create the above problem, that turn this world-condensed symbol monster into the True-Fae-esque shitbag everyone else is talking about. You need to know what you are to control where you are going, and a failure to appreciate one's own monstrosity is one of the classic failings of even the most benign of mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T09:15:05-08:00","id":1056145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1055977#post1055977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're assuming heroes aren't monsters.<br /> <br /> That's a fallacy.<br /> <br /> You're also assuming that just because you are awake, know kung fu, and hang out with a cool chick and bald black guy, you're a hero.<br /> <br /> That's a fallacy.<br /> <br /> You're also assuming that a hero is the best or most desirable thing you can want to be in this world.<br /> <br /> That's a fallacy.<br /> <br /> These are fallacies that transform monsters(read aliens) into monsters(read nightmares). Abandon preconceptions in this world, lest you think the mysteries must be answered instead of transformed into and enlightenment and equanimity be barred from you forever, leaving you trapped in the prison of your self.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh, I disagree. Claiming that anyone with phenomenal power, despite being good and wise, is a monster by definition, is a slippery slope to me. By that definition, God (or Gods) is/are (a) monster(s), since God (or Gods) has/have all of the power in the universe to change anything. The thing that makes the Gods NOT monsters is their Wisdom and Gnosis - their ability to understand when and where to use abilities.<br /> <br /> And if you are totally okay with calling a God a monster, that's where you've lost me, I'm afraid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T09:21:49-08:00","id":1056150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1056145#post1056145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Eh, I disagree. Claiming that anyone with phenomenal power, despite being good and wise, is a monster by definition, is a slippery slope to me. By that definition, God (or Gods) is/are (a) monster(s), since God (or Gods) has/have all of the power in the universe to change anything. The thing that makes the Gods NOT monsters is their Wisdom and Gnosis - their ability to understand when and where to use abilities.<br /> <br /> And if you are totally okay with calling a God a monster, that's where you've lost me, I'm afraid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I've lost you. A god is just a monster you kneel to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T09:43:10-08:00","id":1056159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1056136#post1056136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Free Council actually aren't little-they consistently make up the second largest orders in any given area as a general rule. The Free Council are fucked up for a couple of reasons(like the others), but if you want a classically easy one, &amp;quot;Destroy the Followers of the Lie&amp;quot; is often super easy to cast as &amp;quot;Destroy anyone who disagrees with us.&amp;quot; It happens fairly often.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say they were little; I said there was little to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T09:49:25-08:00","id":1056162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1056043#post1056043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bearing in mind that this is a necroed thread, the last two pages have been pretty much exactly what WHW asked people not to do.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">Michael is right, folks. This thread, though an old one, was made for discussing examples of Mages being monsters, and explicitly not to be another iteration of the same argument of whether Mages are monsters or not. If you want to have that argument again, necro one of the other threads about it or start a new one.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T09:53:48-08:00","id":1056165,"title":"","content":"Lots of misunderstandings we got here, serves me right for just rambling on. To disentanglement!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1056047#post1056047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> .... Yeah, no. First of all, that's not how abuse actually works. Secondly, no, it wasn't a Lie. That sidebar actually refers to the Exarchs and Seers ruling the world, and suggests the Pentacle (and thus the PCs) is at war with them. Not that Sleeper Science is wrong. In fact, for someone who's also a part of Free Council who believes that science is an echo of seeking Supernal Truth? Frankly, I don't see my PC having any qualms with making peace between &quot;newly discovered power&quot; and being a doctor. She had qualms about the people close to her being subject to Long Term Nimbus (thus the Wisdom). But the power itself? Not really.</div> </div> </div> </div>First: Abuse works perfectly fine with the abuser not considering themselves an abuser. Believing they're doing the best for the victim, whom they don't see as a victim but someone they're helping. Whether or not something is abuse is entirely an experience of the one who is in a position of less power.<br /> <br /> I was too vague with the 'a lot of it was a Lie.' You learn that a lot of what a whole hospital has to deal with, short to long-term, could be handled in a few seconds by a single experienced Life mage. Hell, a newb with an imbued item. All the suffering, needless. There be exarchic influence at play.<br /> <br /> I did not mean to imply Sleeper Science is wrong, my bad if it turned out like that.<br /> <br /> And again to the 'Science is not wrong,' did not mean to imply the power is antithetical to being a doctor, but rather that being a doctor, one who deals with injury and illness and all kinds of suffering on a very likely daily basis, it will be exceedingly hard to resist using a tool that can just make it all go away. Not that it's hard to make peace between having/using the power and being a doc, but rather between being a doc with this power and not using it. Which brings Wisdom into play, a mechanic that is on the boundary of preparation and consequence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1056047#post1056047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, choosing to not to help people is not a &quot;monstrous choice.&quot; There's fairly well established ethics in the medical community about responcibility to patients as well as to the self. That's why the Wisdom - the understanding when its best to apply the balance of the personal life and the duties as a doctor and the life as a mage. Its knowing that experimenting on living people is kidn of a bad, immoral thing that shouldn't be done. Its knowing that there are times when casting magic shouldn't be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it is! It's the scale that gets ya, or me as it were XD<br /> It's not a monstrous choice to not help that specific person in that specific situation. It is a monstrous choice to have power on a dramatic scale and not use it to help people.<br /> <br /> Certainly ethics of medical practice is very important, and while I am not informed enough to go into detail, I don't really have to. Medical ethics is by necessity formed by medical professionals in context of what medicine can do, and the consequences thereof.<br /> As a code I can only presume is quite ingrained into doctors during their training, what happens to that when your tools to heal suddenly surpass your previous ones by leaps and bounds? But also come with different risks - specifically patients' integrity breaking points if they witness the healing, and forgetting or rationalising parts of it if exposed to it.<br /> <br /> So you are now a medical ethics panel of one, because telling sleepers is a no-no. And informed consent is very tricky, if at all possible even in a roundabout way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1056047#post1056047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third, &quot;wanting to help people&quot; is not a cliche. I went into social services because I want to help people in real life. Its called &quot;this actually happens with a lot of frequency.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies if this was offensive, but yes it is. By definition, because it's very much overused in fiction.<br /> I did mean specifically in fiction, as per talking about a Mage game, in real life it's obviously much more meaningful, but that it happens a lot is what makes it a fictional clichee, certainly not the first or last one to be important and good in real life.<br /> <br /> <br /> Power corrupts has been scientifically proven false? Not being facetious here, please link to the studies, I'm very interested, in PM if it's too off-topic here.<br /> Because I don't see it that way for CofD. If studies show it, that's delightful for us, but I'll be throwing that out wholesale for the World of Darkness, or Chronicles thereof.<br /> <br /> I see you're trying to find monstrousness in mechanics, and I'm fine with it not being there. Not the way you want it to be.<br /> <br /> Also significantly, a Changeling can be a not-monster. Because why not? There's addiction to Glamour, easily sated through positive dreams and periodic nomnoms of positive emotions from someone you care about and who knows about this ... and there's what else? Being hunted. Being a victim. The powers of the wyrd are, as you say, ripe for abuse (but much less so than Mage ones), but do not equal abuse perpetrated, even more so than for Mages.<br /> <br /> Vampires too, mind. They need blood to live, but hey, blood is not a thing in scarcity. Put some Merit dots on character creation into a loving family that knows about vampirism and provides blood enough to live. The vamp then follows the path of humanity in whatever version or edition you want.<br /> <br /> It's certainly much easier for mages, if the only thing you consider are the punishment mechanics. We seem to disagree strongly here, but I am much in love with the 2E orientation away from punishment mechanics, and going towards rewards of story/experience Beats and willpower and whatnot.<br /> <br /> I will again point out my favored fluff, which is addicted to Mysteries. Your proposal of the Obsessed Condition works quite nicely too. Even if it's less of a stick than you mentioned wanting to the carrot of Beats and Mana. Consider perhaps the Addicted series of Conditions.<br /> <br /> Final thoughts: They're not inherently monsters. But they're immensely powerful humans. So very likely to become monsters in the CofD. Even/especially if they don't see themselves that way, or even any of their Awakened peers.<br /> <br /> Turns out I have many thoughts on this and they're less coherent than I'd like. More to follow I'm sure <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11842,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","user":"Aeryes","date":". 02-28-2017, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T10:08:13-08:00","id":1056176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jim Butcher, Ghost Story</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cOh,&quot; the girl said, shaking her head. &quot;Don't be so simple. People adore monsters. They fill their songs and stories with them. They define themselves in relation to them. You know what a monster is, young shade? Power. Power and choice. Monsters make choices. Monsters shape the world. Monsters force us to become stronger, smarter, better. They sift the weak from the strong and provide a forge for the steeling of souls. Even as we curse monsters, we admire them. Seek to become them, in some ways.&quot; Her eyes became distant. &quot;There are far, far worse things to be than a monster.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the ultraquick and brief intervention, but i just had to post it. Also, loving the arguments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:38:38-08:00","id":1056243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1056176#post1056176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry for the ultraquick and brief intervention, but i just had to post it. Also, loving the arguments.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my favorite bits from that series. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T14:36:48-08:00","id":1056324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1056165#post1056165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of misunderstandings we got here, serves me right for just rambling on. To disentanglement!</div> </div> </div> </div> Or I just flat out disagree with you. Because its not a misunderstanding when I just disagree the very basis of your stance. To sum it up, a lot of your statements are nothing more than your personal opinions that I don't agree with. Especially on your definitions of &quot;monster.&quot; I'm going to just hit the high notes, and leave this to lie instead of going over everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First: Abuse works perfectly fine with the abuser not considering themselves an abuser. Believing they're doing the best for the victim, whom they don't see as a victim but someone they're helping. Whether or not something is abuse is entirely an experience of the one who is in a position of less power. </div> </div> </div> Actually, you said, and I quote, &quot;<i>that </i><i>level of power is inherently abusive.&quot; </i>I call BS on it; everything else you have to say about abuse is meaningless unless you can prove this. Power, on itself, is not never inherently abusive. It has potential for abuse, but potential abuse is not actual abuse.<br /> <br /> So, unless you can prove that mages are inherantly abusive in some way, everything that follows is just your way of running the game, and not actually part of the default setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because I don't see it that way for CofD. </div> </div> </div> Here's a fun fact. No where in Mage 2e does it say that having power is corruptive. Mages might be hubristic, but that's not the same thing as corrupt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also significantly, a Changeling can be a not-monster. Because why not? </div> </div> </div> Because we're back to trying to define &quot;monster&quot; again. I don't agree with the one you're using, and I'm going to leave it at that. This is not the thread for that discussion.<br /> <br /> And with that, I'm done. Mages are monsters as a direct result of Paradox, Nimbus, and Obsessions. These mechanics could use more teeth for my games, but they do work. As far as I see, everything else either flows from these three, or is just other individual tables' personal settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-28-2017, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T15:22:17-08:00","id":1056340,"title":"","content":"A few fun examples of monstrosity that have occured in my last few games are:<br /> <br /> - Tearing the Goetia of someone's affections for another person out of their mind, because they thought that relationship was weighing the other person down<br /> - Disguising oneself as another person, the living their life with their family for the next day, building up their hopes that the person had changed by acting strangely nice, then simply leaving without an explanation<br /> - Sending an ephemeral entity off to kidnap children so you could sacrifice them for mana<br /> - Mind-controlling civilians to kill Seer agents, simultaneously enhancing their mental attributes so they have a better chance of coming out of Quiescence unscathed<br /> - Inuring Devouring the Slain, then repeating its use, combined with Mend, upon an unconscious individual within the mage's own Demesne, to reap ludicrous amounts of mana and willpower<br /> - Summoning the Goetia of one's own wrath, and then leaving it alone in a room with someone he completely and utterly hates while the now calm collected Mage goes and has coffee<br /> - Tricking an entire tribe into believing that the hostile nature of a local spirit is their own fault, and that only through appeasing it can they hope to live in harmony, then collecting the boons from that Spirit for finding it a group of follower<br /> - Corrupting a Spirit of Bravery into a spirit of a Selfish Motivation by binding it to a mask and then starving it of Essence until it was at the brink of discorporation/death, and then offering it Essence with increasing amounts of selfish urges over and over.<br /> - Manipulating a Changeling's memories to believe that a) he has a daughter b) that you have kidnapped her and will torture her and potentially hand her over to a privateer if he doesn't do what you want. Thinking he'll be fine when he does what you want, and realises it was all a trick. Not realising how agonising it is to grant him hope tinged with fear, only to strip it all away and leave him with nothing but an aching loss.<br /> <br /> I mean, only couple of those were by PCs.<br /> But I hold out hope for the future.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T23:20:35-08:00","id":1056499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1056087#post1056087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a reminder in the thread that four of the six playable Orders in the core have as tenets that aren't really debated:<br /> <br /> -That anyone who isn't a wizard should absolutely led without question by their wizard masters (who are doing it for their own good, honest).<br /> -That Sleepers should not be allowed near secret knowledge and that, by their inability to Awaken, they've proven themselves unworthy of access to the real truths of the world.<br /> -What the other guy said, but going so far as to spread outright misinformation and lies to try and keep them from Awakening.<br /> -Using your wizardly powers to tilt a conflict to match your personal vision is A-Okay.<br /> <br /> And that's without pointing out that of the two remaining, one looked at Gnosticism and thought the Demiurge was the good guy, and the other is only hard to say anything bad about because there's <i>so little to them</i>; the Libertines are like a sewing circle for people who disagree with Atlantean dogma and think that democracy is real neato, but they still maintain the Veil and manipulate Sleeper societies.<br /> <br /> Wizards don't need in-built features to be monstrous; just give a chimpanzee a box of hand grenades and nature sorts itself out.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bJust damn/thread. Mages are monsters because as far as I see they are the only humans in the setting to have actual real choice with parameters Donald Trump and other mundane types fantasize about. Though not even a Silver Ladder mage is arrogant or dumb enough to be President of the United States despite the access to levels of pure power most regular people recognize but refuse to accept or admit. And Seers and all that angle of course.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's kind of like the Seers and Silver Ladder are fighting about who runs the Executive Branch and Senate and the Free Council is all about being in control of the Supreme Court and the House of Representatives. Except the Seers don't give a fuck about whoever wants something different from their personal desires and the Silver Ladder invented and are the Supreme Court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 03-01-2017, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T02:03:07-08:00","id":1056539,"title":"","content":"Mages are monsters, because they will tear your life apart. They'll bring spirits and creatures into your house, they will show you wonders and miracles that could tear your very sanity, and reveal your place at the food chain - not at the top of it, but at the very bottom of another food chain, one you didn't even know you could exist. The thing is, even if the Pentacle wins the War (the War like that), they'll open the door to a new Universe of choices, and dangers, and responsabilities. A new, horrifiyng, powerful, more Real Universe. If the Seers are the ones to win the War, they'll cripple humanity for all eternity. One way of another, they'll destroy who you are, right now. That speaks monster to me. Some mages fight the good fight, but that good fight will destroy you nonetheless. Is that not terrifying? Bring Beast to this discusion, and you'll see a lot of mages as Anakim <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My pleasure, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> . Is one of my favourites too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T05:09:49-08:00","id":1056571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href