te":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T06:12:36-08:00","id":1056602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1056571#post1056571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAnakim, that's a Mummy thing?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Beast: the Primodrial</b> one - it's name of 'Giants' Family of monsters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T07:08:44-08:00","id":1056620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1056324#post1056324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Or I just flat out disagree with you. Because its not a misunderstanding when I just disagree the very basis of your stance. To sum it up, a lot of your statements are nothing more than your personal opinions that I don't agree with. Especially on your definitions of &quot;monster.&quot; I'm going to just hit the high notes, and leave this to lie instead of going over everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Disagreements and misunderstandings both (misunderstanding mostly in the Science thing, and doc + power thing).<br /> We disagree on what is monstrous, so leaving that there. <br /> <br /> All in all, I agree with you that &quot;inherently abusive&quot; is too strong for Mages at lower power levels (and iffy at higher levels). I also have no plans in defending this to any objective standard, so you're right in this just being the way I view the setting.<br /> <br /> You can be truly Wise if you focus on this. And depending on definitions and whatevs, Mages don't have to be monsters.<br /> <br /> Beef up those teeth in your games, sounds like you'll enjoy it better that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T16:56:42-08:00","id":1056855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1056539#post1056539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages are monsters, because they will tear your life apart. They'll bring spirits and creatures into your house, they will show you wonders and miracles that could tear your very sanity, and reveal your place at the food chain - not at the top of it, but at the very bottom of another food chain, one you didn't even know you could exist. The thing is, even if the Pentacle wins the War (the War like that), they'll open the door to a new Universe of choices, and dangers, and responsabilities. A new, horrifiyng, powerful, more Real Universe. If the Seers are the ones to win the War, they'll cripple humanity for all eternity. One way of another, they'll destroy who you are, right now. That speaks monster to me. Some mages fight the good fight, but that good fight will destroy you nonetheless. Is that not terrifying? Bring Beast to this discusion, and you'll see a lot of mages as Anakim <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My pleasure, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> . Is one of my favourites too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Heck, the Anakim Stereotype on Mages literally says exactly that: &quot;You know how I say that not all giants tower over you physically? That's these guys.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T15:43:27-08:00","id":1057789,"title":"","content":"I usually play Hunter, while dabbling in other splats, so the concept of &quot;at what point are you a monster yourself&quot; is very near and dear to me. On top of that, you've also given me an idea for a new antagonist for my Mage Hunters but that's just how my warped Hunter mind sees things now \ud83d\ude00. I'd say what really makes a Mage a monster is their separation from mortal thinking. A vampire thinks in the terms of a predator, with the beast altering their perceptions of the world around them as they grow more callous towards mortals, werewolves start to think more like spirits like one werewolf pack I made for a friend who's totem had them going out and slashing people's tires and vandalizing property for the spirit's amusement and they saw themselves as perfectly noble, even as their totem pushed them towards the pure and made them more beast than man. Likewise mages just don't think like normal people anymore and thoughts like &quot;I can just undo it&quot; will pretty much always crop up sooner or later, and I find among many Mage players that I've met a certain amount of &quot;all you have is a hammer&quot; mentality. What I mean by that is that they get addicted to using magic to solve problems and start to only think of what new spell they can do to fix a problem, which tends to lead to a large amount of paradox before they know it. Sooner or later their actions are going to hurt people, and just because they can make the consequences disappear doesn't mean they didn't do the action, and as they become more callous they stop caring about the bad they do to those around them, they no longer see it as all that bad compared to other things they've done. It's only a matter of time before their actions catch up with them though.<br /> <br /> In many respects it's similar to Hunters but with even more power perversion potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T23:34:17-08:00","id":1058309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1056602#post1056602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Beast: the Primodrial</b> one - it's name of 'Giants' Family of monsters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bBeast is a pile of shit. A game that makes the Protagonist a Mary Sue? No thanks. I might be able to use that term though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 03-05-2017, 02:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T23:51:43-08:00","id":1058313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/831840-mages-as-monsters-discussion-examples-thinktank?p=1058309#post1058309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bBeast is a pile of shit. A game that makes the Protagonist a Mary Sue? No thanks. I might be able to use that term though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoa, no need for condemning the entire game. Although Beasts can be played as a Mary Sue, the same can be said for playing Mage as a superhero genre or Werewolf a